x; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Exalted Advantage<br /> <br /> The Solar Exalted Advantages are:<br /> <br /> 1. They always win tied rolls.<br /> 2. They don't pay the mote cost for Excellencies. Excellencies are free for Solars.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T08:35:22-07:00","id":1380969,"title":"","content":"Also Getimian Castes are Seasonal which is very interesting.<br /> Heres a tidbit from Neall that goes even more into it.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Spring<br /> The Vernals are heroic dreamers, warrior poets, and guardians. They helped make their world beautiful \u2014 and now Creation will benefit from their bold vision.<br /> <br /> Summer<br /> The Estivals are conquerors, mad prophets, and iconoclasts who upend the old orders. They come from worlds of upheaval, ready to shatter the old ways of Creation.<br /> <br /> Autumn<br /> The Autumnals are inspirational war-leaders, healers, and saviors. They come from worlds redeemed by their sacrifices; now they will redeem Creation, as well.<br /> <br /> Winter<br /> The Hibernals are magicians, demiurges, and powerbrokers who transform society. They come from worlds made orderly and grand, with the strength of will to make whole what Creation has set asunder. </div> </div> </div>Also in a discussion someone pointed out how Exalted Seasons don't match up to are standard ones. It's all about the elements. I find that detail interesting.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T08:39:56-07:00","id":1380971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1380962#post1380962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Exalted Advantage<br /> <br /> The Solar Exalted Advantages are:<br /> <br /> 1. They always win tied rolls.<br /> 2. They don't pay the mote cost for Excellencies. Excellencies are free for Solars.</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Same, I'm interested that while they didn't really go with Supernal(probably to open it up more for Abyssals and Infernals in variety) but I'm just fond how they still found a way to capture Solars. Especially the win ties one. That it just the Protagonist power if I ever saw one. And with the straight-lining of the power levels and maxing the dice around 20, I expect to see a lot more ties under Essence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T08:57:25-07:00","id":1380984,"title":"","content":"Stuff!<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Essence sounds pretty interesting overall. I'm someone who generally enjoys both Exalted's setting and 3e's system, but the idea of a system that's simpler and more accessible is nice. The way Exalt types are seemingly mostly differentiated from one another by Universal Charm modifiers, exclusive Charms, and Exalt Advantages sounds like it'll be neat. The Sidereal Advantages also give me hope for 3e Sidereals making astrology easier to handle. The way they're squashing the power curve is also nice and makes sense for a simplified game, honestly.<br /> <br /> I already knew much of the Infernal stuff already (in that rather than being catalyzed by failure they're catalyzed by being downtrodden, broken, and angry at the world) but the specific note of their revolutionary flavor was nice. Devil-Body (replacing the old 3e Infernal preview's take on Shintai) sounds interesting as a sort of super-mode where some Charms work better/differently/cheaper. I think the mention of Demonic Form from Demon: the Descent is enticing and sounds like there's going to be fun room for customization.<br /> <br /> Getimians getting their first big infodump, plus Neall's offerings on the Discord that Iceblade has transcribed, give us a better picture of them now and I'm into it. Specifying that they're basically heroes of possible fate-threads that didn't make it to the Loom and a lot of their stuff ties back to their sort of alt-Creation makes me very excited to get my hands on them eventually.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Overall, whether I end up playing it or not, I already have solid interest in Essence just as sort of a preview of things that will later come to 3e proper.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T08:58:25-07:00","id":1380986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1380962#post1380962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Exalted Advantage<br /> <br /> The Solar Exalted Advantages are:<br /> <br /> 1. They always win tied rolls.<br /> 2. They don't pay the mote cost for Excellencies. Excellencies are free for Solars.</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Wow that's pretty big. If they lose Supernal though its probably required.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T09:22:51-07:00","id":1380989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1380969#post1380969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also Getimian Castes are Seasonal which is very interesting.<br /> Heres a tidbit from Neall that goes even more into it.</div> </div> </div> </div>He also spoiled Getimian animas:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Anima<br /> Getimian animas are pale rainbows mixed with black and white Essence. At the active level, this anima surrounds them, either ever-flowing or perfectly tranquil. At the iconic level, it bursts outwards, becoming a web of unrealized possibilities. Vistas from the Getimian\u2019s world can be seen within \u2014 as can scuttling pattern spiders, seeking to reshape Creation in that world\u2019s image.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T09:32:32-07:00","id":1380992,"title":"","content":"Solar Excellency trick makes sense if you compress splats to have similar dice limits, and you are possibly having same mote pools between splats (?) and you want Solars still to be rolling more dice and winning most roll-offs (&quot;They're excellent!&quot;). I wonder if there will be other limits to Excellencies to dissuade players from throwing down full Excellencies, or if it would effectively be Solars always rolling a very high pool?<br /> <br /> So Getimians = Sliders from parallel universes or something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T09:37:56-07:00","id":1380995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1380992#post1380992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Getimians = Sliders from parallel universes or something?</div> </div> </div> </div>More heroes from worlds that might have been, given existence by Exaltation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":51,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","user":"marin","date":". 04-13-2020, 12:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T09:53:18-07:00","id":1381001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1380986#post1380986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wow that's pretty big. If they lose Supernal though its probably required.</div> </div> </div> </div>They also then immediately stated &quot;if you're thinking this means they'll always throw full Excellency on everything because why not, the way Excellencies work in Essence is different so it shakes out differently than you think.&quot;<br /> <br /> Which makes me extra interested to see how stuff actually does work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T09:54:38-07:00","id":1381002,"title":"","content":"Wait hold up<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Getimians are from another reality?! Oh, dang, I may have to rewrite a few concepts but this has POTENTIAL!</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T09:57:43-07:00","id":1381004,"title":"","content":"Getimians are heroes who might have been, and, being heroes, they would have changed the world. Then they're realized by the Getimian Exaltation in Creation, where, never having existed, they never made any changes. So you might have a woman who, as a mighty warrior-politician, united all the kingdoms of the South into a great empire and threw off the yoke of the Realm, only to suddenly awaken one day to a world where nothing she accomplished ever happened because she was never born. From Creation's perspective she popped into existence from nowhere; from her own perspective she's lost in a new world where none of her friends or lovers or allies remember her and some might also not exist. And maybe her two best friends are mortal enemies or something.<br /> <br /> They're not from, like, sci-fi alternates or anything. The divergence point is generally their own birth. I am saying this now because I can see people getting really excited about playing visitors from Exalted Modern and I know that sort of thing is brain candy for folks and I'd hate to see everyone disappointed when it doesn't happen.<br /> <br /> (Also they're all sufficiently mighty heroes to make lasting changes to Creation <i>as mortals</i>, without Exalting.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":229,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","user":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","date":". 04-13-2020, 01:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T10:11:15-07:00","id":1381008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1381004#post1381004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> (Also they're all sufficiently mighty heroes to make lasting changes to Creation <i>as mortals</i>, without Exalting.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is very cool. As much as I see it that Exalts should be the main play type it's still awesome seeing mortals making an impact on the setting or being able to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T10:18:50-07:00","id":1381010,"title":"","content":"For context on my own post on this, implied with that comment was &quot;Figuratively, Sliders... from soap-bubble possibility alternate universes without too much divergence from mainline Creation&quot;, and not &quot;Literally.... from actual, still very-much-independently existing very divergent worlds&quot;. <br /> <br /> (I mean, I hope it was implied and I don't generally come across as that actually clueless!).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T10:50:42-07:00","id":1381020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1381010#post1381010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For context on my own post on this, implied with that comment was &quot;Figuratively, Sliders... from soap-bubble possibility alternate universes without too much divergence from mainline Creation&quot;, and not &quot;Literally.... from actual, still very-much-independently existing very divergent worlds&quot;.<br /> <br /> (I mean, I hope it was implied and I don't generally come across as that actually clueless!).</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope I didn't come across as &quot;blaming you&quot; for &quot;getting it wrong&quot; or something; so little has been said about Getimians it's only natural for people to wildly speculate now that something is being said. It's just that, even now, I recall the Lunar Illusionists debacle, and I'd hate to see everyone fall in love, with and make character concepts they're eager to play, a version of them that's invented on the forum and doesn't reflect what they'll be when they're out.<br /> <br /> For context, if there's anyone who doesn't know what I'm talking about, the First Edition corebook has a line about Lunars being &quot;peerless illusionists&quot; or something close to that, which people took to mean they'd be raising up phantoms and casting illusion spells. Then the actual book came out and they were only illusionists in the sense that they were capable of transforming themselves into snakes and then when you pick them up to admire them because you love snakes they transform back into themselves and should &quot;Rar, it's me!&quot; and then stab you. And the resulting arguments and bitterness about not being able to play this character I'd imagined kinda contributed to the developer leaving the forums, where he'd previously posted profusely. I am confident that when Getimians see print it'll be in overall in a much better format than 1e Lunars (which had problems besides that, partially because the originally-contracted Charm writer had to pull out of the project last minute due to health problems and so the Charms were written in a rush by someone less familiar with the rules), but still, those arguments haunt me, and I am still to this day deathly afraid of the results of people falling in love with a promise I made accidentally. And Getimians as visitors from other worlds in the sense of the Endless Corridor from Castlevania Season 3 strikes me as that sort of promise that people could fall in love with. So, you know, just nipping this in the bud.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":229,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","user":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","date":". 04-13-2020, 01:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T11:09:17-07:00","id":1381027,"title":"","content":"No problem, it makes sense! I'm myself just trying to clear up that I was not in the first place suggesting literally something which... well, I was probably harsh calling it &quot;dumb&quot; (it could well be rich with possibility when well executed by somebody!), but which would probably open sufficient unwanted cans of worms as to probably be a pretty chaotic hand-grenade to lob into the middle of the canon setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T11:39:12-07:00","id":1381038,"title":"","content":"I'll be honest, I wasn't really interested in Getimians until now, but this sounds pretty cool. Especially as we do a lot of stuff with parallel worlds and crossovers...<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, the most interesting thing for me wasn't really the spoilers, but rather what they've been thinking about dice pools, difficulties, how these things actually come out in games. And I think it's actually good that Dixie hadn't played Exalted, and so the writers had to justify things to her; it's worth challenging long-held assumptions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 04-13-2020, 02:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T11:41:58-07:00","id":1381042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1381038#post1381038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll be honest, I wasn't really interested in Getimians until now, but this sounds pretty cool. Especially as we do a lot of stuff with parallel worlds and crossovers...<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, the most interesting thing for me wasn't really the spoilers, but rather what they've been thinking about dice pools, difficulties, how these things actually come out in games. And I think it's actually good that Monica hadn't played Exalted, and so the writers had to justify things to her; it's worth challenging long-held assumptions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quick correction, Monica has played a ton of Exalted. Dixie is the one who hasn't.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my RPG podcast: <a href=\"http://thestorytold.libsyn.com\" target=\"_blank\">The Story Told</a><br /> Follow my ongoing Exalted Campaign: <a href=\"https://thefallofjiara.obsidianportal.com/adventure-log\" target=\"_blank\">The Fall of Jiara</a><br /> Check out my Community Content: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Chazz%20Kellner\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....hazz%20Kellner</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/702-elfspeaker","name":"ElfSpeaker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar702_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T11:51:55-07:00","id":1381049,"title":"","content":"Ah, sorry! I'll edit that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"k