"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T12:56:13-07:00","id":1381066,"title":"","content":"Did any of you catch how long the book will be? I think they mentioned it very briefly, while talking about how long the Fangs at the Gate and What Fire Has Wrought charm sections were.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T13:03:33-07:00","id":1381070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1381066#post1381066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did any of you catch how long the book will be? I think they mentioned it very briefly, while talking about how long the Fangs at the Gate and What Fire Has Wrought charm sections were.</div> </div> </div> </div>About 150k words, I think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T13:19:22-07:00","id":1381073,"title":"","content":"How long is that compared to the other books?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T13:54:32-07:00","id":1381083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1381073#post1381073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How long is that compared to the other books?</div> </div> </div> </div>Longer than Arms or The Realm, shorter than the 3e splatbooks. Little over the usual 2e splatbook.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T14:07:07-07:00","id":1381089,"title":"","content":"I'm hoping we'll get a companion book with the Kickstarter!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my RPG podcast: <a href=\"http://thestorytold.libsyn.com\" target=\"_blank\">The Story Told</a><br /> Follow my ongoing Exalted Campaign: <a href=\"https://thefallofjiara.obsidianportal.com/adventure-log\" target=\"_blank\">The Fall of Jiara</a><br /> Check out my Community Content: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Chazz%20Kellner\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....hazz%20Kellner</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/702-elfspeaker","name":"ElfSpeaker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar702_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T14:26:56-07:00","id":1381095,"title":"","content":"that would indeed be cool, allow some expansion but nothing else from that","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T14:28:01-07:00","id":1381096,"title":"","content":"Now I understand how the Getimian Exalted are supposed to be like Organization 13's named Nobodies from <i>Kingdom Hearts</i>. A person just spontaneously appears in the world with an entire life's worth of memories and strong magical powers... but with no real identity or place within the world, as far as the world is concerned.<br /> <br /> But they don't have Somebodies or any feelings about not having feelings, since they clearly have feelings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T14:37:50-07:00","id":1381098,"title":"","content":"Neall's thoughts about being burnt out on playing Exalted sounds just like mine, so him finding it revitalising is quite encouraging!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 04-13-2020, 05:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T14:59:14-07:00","id":1381109,"title":"","content":"I'm really happy to find out Getiminians seems closer to heroes than anti-heroes. The Getiminians look we had from 3e Core Book made them seem very ... oriented to be only anti-hero of the Sidereal, which didn't interest me as much as this new explanation","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T15:14:29-07:00","id":1381113,"title":"","content":"I'm wondering if they're still Yin-Yang themed, as John Morke talked back. Not sure that's been mentioned at all in these spoilers?<br /> <br /> Because if so, their 2 patrons are definitely the Ebon Dragon and Scarlet Queen. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T15:57:51-07:00","id":1381123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1381113#post1381113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm wondering if they're still Yin-Yang themed, as John Morke talked back. Not sure that's been mentioned at all in these spoilers?<br /> <br /> Because if so, their 2 patrons are definitely the Ebon Dragon and Scarlet Queen. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>They are but they are not calling them Yin and Yang.<br /> <br /> Neall dropped that Spring and Summer are flowing while Autumn and Winter are still, for whatever that means","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":3742,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","user":"Iceblade44","date":". 04-13-2020, 07:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T16:50:12-07:00","id":1381138,"title":"","content":"I wouldn\u2019t call those terms settled yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my RPG podcast: <a href=\"http://thestorytold.libsyn.com\" target=\"_blank\">The Story Told</a><br /> Follow my ongoing Exalted Campaign: <a href=\"https://thefallofjiara.obsidianportal.com/adventure-log\" target=\"_blank\">The Fall of Jiara</a><br /> Check out my Community Content: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Chazz%20Kellner\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....hazz%20Kellner</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/702-elfspeaker","name":"ElfSpeaker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar702_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T17:40:13-07:00","id":1381151,"title":"","content":"I heard the part about where PC Solars get to break ties against NPC Solars, and that's fine, but it doesn't seem strictly necessary to me.<br /> <br /> The PC Solar still enjoys the tie-breaker Advantage... in that they get to enjoy negating that Advantage in their opponent where no one else could.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T18:18:27-07:00","id":1381161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1381151#post1381151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I heard the part about where PC Solars get to break ties against NPC Solars, and that's fine, but it doesn't seem strictly necessary to me.<br /> <br /> The PC Solar still enjoys the tie-breaker Advantage... in that they get to enjoy negating that Advantage in their opponent where no one else could.</div> </div> </div> </div>There may be a general principle where PCs get to break ties against NPCs when Solars aren't involved, and this is just continuing that - if opposed rolls often don't have a good outcome in the case of ties, that could be a reasonable solution to avoid them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T19:50:59-07:00","id":1381189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1381161#post1381161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There may be a general principle where PCs get to break ties against NPCs when Solars aren't involved, and this is just continuing that - if opposed rolls often don't have a good outcome in the case of ties, that could be a reasonable solution to avoid them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Excellent point!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T20:53:52-07:00","id":1381204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1381109#post1381109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm really happy to find out Getiminians seems closer to heroes than anti-heroes. The Getiminians look we had from 3e Core Book made them seem very ... oriented to be only anti-hero of the Sidereal, which didn't interest me as much as this new explanation</div> </div> </div> </div>Me, I can see the Best of Both Worlds option.<br /> <br /> They <i>are </i>heroes from an alternate time. They are<i> also</i> alien invaders, from dimensions stranger than Malfeas, and no way to get back - so they're going to make Creation<i> their </i>world.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Oh Sol, I just realized; an all-Getiminian Circle is quite possibly a bunch of <i>isekai </i>main characters, and Rakan Thulio is an excellent potential &quot;god who guides you to your new realm.&quot; Behold, the Rising of the Seasonal Hero.<br /> <br /> EDIT2: I just listened to the interview. Apparently, 2E Green Sun Princes draw on Demon: The <i>Descent </i>for inspiration.<br /> <br /> Please tell me this makes them, at least in part, the Other Magitech Exalts? Please? I wanna drive my Hellstrider.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 04-14-2020, 12:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T21:17:52-07:00","id":1381206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1381204#post1381204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please tell me this makes them, at least in part, the Other Magitech Exalts? Please? I wanna drive my Hellstrider.</div> </div> </div> </div>How in Creation is a Hellstrider meaningfully different from a warstrider made by a Solar sorcerer who bound demons into the chassis? If it's not meaningfully different, why the distinction?<br /> <br /> \u200bIf something like Karvara can exist and is still called a warstrider, then I posit that an Infernal versions of these walking war-machines should also be called warstriders.<br /> <br /> \u200b(I also feel that warstriders both are and should be rare enough that having an entire sub-class of them diminishes the concept. <i>A</i> necromantic warstrider made with soulsteel and mammoth bones is cool - if seven entirely unaffiliated entities have them, necessitating coining the term &quot;bonestrider,&quot; then <i>it's less cool.</i>)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 04-14-2020, 12:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T22:00:25-07:00","id":1381210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1381206#post1381206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How in Creation is a Hellstrider meaningfully different from a warstrider made by a Solar sorcerer who bound demons into the chassis? If it's not meaningfully different, why the distinction?</div> </div> </div> </div>From what I understand, a Hellstrider actually is a demon, or rather several, remade into the living internal frame of a much larger armor; you don't pilot one so much as guide it. It's a mount, not a robot. They also seem a bit easier to repair, since a lot of their architecture heals on its own.<br /> <br /> More importantly, they're much, much easier to make, so one showing up doesn't need its own backstory - it could be a brand new one, which fits the new Infernals as &quot;heralds of revolution&quot; (since this Infernal has created something that should be a relic of times long gone). Making one seems a lot more doable for a relatively young Exalt, and since much of the infrastructure exists in Malfeas already, it seems like making one is more of the start of a story than the climax of one.<br /> <br /> Most importantly, relative ease = more of them, which means more potential stories wherein multiple sides have Hellstriders or equivalent forces, which really suits the more war-torn nature of Malfeas. Also, since Hellstriders are characters in their own right, that leads to even more potential stories about finding a balance between their wants and their pilots'.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I posted this before seeing the edit. Karvara's existence is a point, but he's also N/A; not something you can get out of the gate. I do agree that, even if the core technique is repeatable, every Hellstrider should be a unique creation, same as any other warstrider. In fact, I say that the twice-unique nature should be emphasized, because not only is every Hellstrider a unique character, they're born at least partly from a unique set of demons blended together, and building one in the place of simply getting some neomah to make a really big unique demon or bribing a behemoth needs their own personal reason. Hell, even typing this, I have an idea for a demon lord that <i>is </i>a Hellstrider; she was born, in true Evangelion fashion, from a human woman letting Alveua reforge her soul into the core intellect of one to protect her family, and now she maintains her portion of the layer by guiding pilot-viceroys to unlock her Evocations.<br /> <br /> EDIT2: To clarify; the idea is &quot;lower barrier to entry&quot; not &quot;less special.&quot; Believe me, I'm just using &quot;Hellstrider&quot; for ease of reference; they are still warstriders, they just have Evocations based on their components. I doubt if many new ones were made before the return of the Solars, especially since demons don't generally pilot them. I think the analogy I'm going for is that a Hellstrider is very much a Second Age innovation on the basic idea of a warstrider; the old techniques and wonderworking is gone now, but demons are still bindable, and it's simpler in theory to put armor on a very big demon than it is to make pure armor walk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 04-14-2020, 01:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T22:05:37-07:00","id":1381211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1381210#post1381210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what I understand, a Hellstrider actually is a demon, or rather several, remade into the living internal frame of a much larger armor...</div> </div> </div> </div>...and Karvara actually is a behemoth, remade into the living internal frame of a giant suit of armor.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1381210#post1381210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">you don't pilot one so much as guide it. It's a mount, not a robot.</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet in 2e, the person sitting in the cockpit of a hellstrider is called a <i>pilot</i>, and there's no indication that you can use Ride Charms on this &quot;mount.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1381210#post1381210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They also seem a bit easier to repair, since a lot of their architecture heals on its own.</div> </div> </div> </div>And Karvara possesses Evocations to let it heal as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1381210#post1381210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More importantly, they're much, much easier to make...</div> </div> </div> </div>I dispute the notion that they <i>should </i>be easier to make.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1381210#post1381210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, since Hellstriders are characters in their own right, that leads to even more potential stories about finding a balance between their wants and their pilots'.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>So is Karvara and it's <b>still</b> a warstrider</i>. Karvara has Intimacies and a Resolve score. Karvara breaks free of its pilot's control and acts of its own volition when the pilot Limit Breaks. All the <i>cool </i>things about hellstriders from 2e are present already and the thing that has them is still called a warstrider.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 04-14-2020, 01:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T22:13:38-07:00","id":1381214,"title":"","content":"Which brings us to the question of whether the Juggernaut should be a Warstrider in 3e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T22:21:57-07:00","id":1381217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1381211#post1381211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...and Karvara actually is a behemoth, remade into the living internal frame of a giant suit of armor.</div> </div> </div> </div>See my edits for my refinement of the post. To reiterate, I just want &quot;Hellstrider&quot; (or perhaps more accurately, Malfean Warstrider) rules as a way to get on the action of building them with relatively younger characters in a setting where more warstriders make sense (since Malfeas has a lot of knowledge left over from the First Age and plenty of demonic smiths), not to demean the concept of warstriders. Along with potential refinements to make it clear that yes, the fact your armor has a mind of its own makes driving it a bit different (such as, potentially, a mortal being able to attune to it if the demon likes the pilot).<br /> <br /> To be clear, I was just using &quot;Hellstrider&quot; as a term for &quot;warstrider with demons partly driving it, because they are part of its circuits.&quot; Sorry for the confusion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 04-14-2020, 01:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T22:29:18-07:00","id":1381220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1381217#post1381217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To reiterate, I just want &quot;Hellstrider&quot; (or perhaps more accurately, Malfean Warstrider) rules as a way to get on the action of building them with relatively younger characters in a setting where more warstriders make sense (since Malfeas has a lot of knowledge left over from the First Age and plenty of demonic smiths), not to demean the concept of warstriders.</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet the presence of a warstrider is intended to be a game-changer. The devs suggested that an Exalt strapping into Ascendant Nova Phoenix would be equipped to duel Ligier. And I don't doubt that All-Conquering Colossus or the Cathedral of Sublime Annihilation would probably give him a run for his money as well.<br /> <br /> \u200bI don't feel that kind of firepower should be more commonplace in Malfeas <i>even if</i> techniques exist to bind demons into the chassis of a walking war machine. That shit <i>should</i> be difficult, and an Infernal who makes one should feel really accomplished about it.<br /> <br /> \u200bEspecially considering that making them easier to build just raises the question of why the Exalted bothered building warstriders if hellstriders are just that much easier.<br /> <br /> <b>\u200bThat said...</b><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1381210#post1381210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hell, even typing this, I have an idea for a demon lord that <i>is </i>a Hellstrider; she was born, in true Evangelion fashion, from a human woman letting Alveua reforge her soul into the core intellect of one to protect her family, and now she maintains her portion of the layer by guiding pilot-viceroys to unlock her Evocations.</div> </div> </div> </div>This? This is <i>\u200bso </i>cool. I want that in <i>my</i> game. <i>But</i> please understand why having dozens or hundreds of 'striders littering the Demon City diminishes how cool <i>this</i>\u200b is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 04-14-2020, 01:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T22:29:38-07:00","id":1381221,"title":"","content":"I figure that the rules can fully support a Hellstrider, if by which you mean &quot;Uses Warstrider Rules, but its Evocations are particularly demonic&quot;<br /> <br /> Maybe with Orichalcum as the binding agent holding the demons in place, for purposes of Resonance.<br /> <br /> Edit: And I wouldn't make it available out of the gates unless it were the major focus on the campaign, as Warstriders are also hella powerful and game-defining.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T22:35:40-07:00","id":1381223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1381221#post1381221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Warstriders are... hella powerful and game-defining.</div> </div> </div> </div>I probably should've just said this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T22:37:11-07:00","id":1381225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1381220#post1381220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yet the presence of a warstrider is intended to be a game-changer. The devs suggested that an Exalt strapping into Ascendant Nova Phoenix would be equipped to duel Ligier. And I don't doubt that All-Conquering Colossus or the Cathedral of Sublime Annihilation would probably give him a run for his money as well.<br /> <br /> \u200bI don't feel that kind of firepower should be more commonplace in Malfeas <i>even if</i> techniques exist to bind demons into the chassis of a walking war machine. That shit <i>should</i> be difficult, and an Infernal who makes one should feel really accomplished about it.<br /> <br /> \u200bEspecially considering that making them easier to build just raises the question of why the Exalted bothered building warstriders if hellstriders are just that much easier.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, that makes sense. Truth is, I forgot how much of a power boost warstriders got this edition, and rechecking Arms...yep. Each one is unique for a reason.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the compliment, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 04-14-2020, 01:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T22:39:42-07:00","id":1381227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1381214#post1381214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which brings us to the question of whether the Juggernaut should be a Warstrider in 3e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, <i>to the best of my understanding</i>, Juggernaut is not piloted by one person. His motions are the aggregate result of countless nemissaries using their possession-magic on as much of his corpse-body as they possibly can and directing his shattered limbs to drag himself along, hobbled as he is by the inauspicious citadel on his back.<br /> <br /> I'd use something more like Mahicara to represent him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T22:47:20-07:00","id":1381229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1381225#post1381225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, that makes sense. Truth is, I forgot how much of a power boost warstriders got this edition, and rechecking Arms...yep. Each one is unique for a reason.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the compliment, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, hey, no problem. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T23:42:11-07:00","id":1381238,"title":"","content":"Juggernaut is also commonly described in a scale vastly larger than any warstrider to date, unless you count the Daystar. From the descriptions we get of it well over a thousand feet, even crawling, would be my guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T00:30:35-07:00","id":1381240,"title":"","content":"There's a route you can go with Hellstriders if you want them to be fairly common.<br /> <br /> In my house rules I reimagined the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/27912-lioness-ramblings?p=1249103#post1249103\">Bonestrider</a> as essentially a form of piloted undead megafauna that The Seven-Degreed Physician of Black Maladies has started selling to threshold kingdoms, but in contrast to a true Warstrider that synergises with it's pilot the Bonestrider is basically trying to eat the person inside it (it's really just a different set of sums to having a pet Tyrant Lizard which can have a huge impact on mortal scale warfare if it doesn't eat you out of house and home first). <br /> <br /> Anyway, it wouldn't be out of character for Malfeas to have some biomechanical behemoths (I'd be resistant to making them demons of the First Circle unless they had some serious usage limitations) that would be formidable in the turf wars of the demon city but be a meal for the likes of Karvara.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T00:55:23-07:00","id":1381241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1381204#post1381204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Me, I can see the Best of Both Worlds option.<br /> <br /> They <i>are </i>heroes from an alternate time. They are<i> also</i> alien invaders, from dimensions stranger than Malfeas, and no way to get back - so they're going to make Creation<i> their </i>world.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Oh Sol, I just realized; an all-Getiminian Circle is quite possibly a bunch of <i>isekai </i>main characters, and Rakan Thulio is an excellent potential &quot;god who guides you to your new realm.&quot; Behold, the Rising of the Seasonal Hero.<br /> <br /> EDIT2: I just listened to the interview. Apparently, 2E Green Sun Princes draw on Demon: The <i>Descent </i>for inspiration.<br /> <br /> Please tell me this makes them, at least in part, the Other Magitech Exalts? Please? I wanna drive my Hellstrider.</div> </div> </div> </div>I must say I don't know how this will be presented, but that's not at all how I see the premise : Creation is their world as much as this is ours, and they will have an agenda that is drastically influenced from usual characters because they will have seen at least one alternative version of it. <br /> <br /> To clarify what I meant by my initial statement : At first read of Getiminians (and the few bits here), I expected the Getiminians to be anti-sidereal heroes with some spider attached somewhere in their bodies with totally alien motivation, a bit like The God-Machine has plans that makes no sense for anyone but him in the long-term (to make an analogy with another WoD Game), and in particular to piss off Sidereal and disrupt the Wheel of Fate or whatever. Now I discover that it might actually just be a cool hero that rallied the South to rise against The Realm, and wakes up to discover it never happened. From there you can go anywhere. I prefer the second version much more, even if I understand some players wanting to play the first archetype.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T05:38:24-07:00","id":1381293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1381151#post1381151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I heard the part about where PC Solars get to break ties against NPC Solars, and that's fine, but it doesn't seem strictly necessary to me.<br /> <br /> The PC Solar still enjoys the tie-breaker Advantage... in that they get to enjoy negating that Advantage in their opponent where no one else could.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ties on dice rolls in <b>Exalted</b> against a contested roll or a static trait have gone to the defender across three editions; <b>Essence </b>is no different.<br /> <br /> Solars, however, always win ties.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T05:52:20-07:00","id":1381299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1381293#post1381293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ties on dice rolls in <b>Exalted</b> against a contested roll or a static trait have gone to the defender across three editions; <b>Essence </b>is no different.<br /> <br /> Solars, however, always win ties.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess this is obvious, but just to be sure : ties between 2 solars go for the defender ? <br /> <br /> (Also I might be confused right now, but if I attack someone that has 2 Defense on 3e, and roll 2 successes on the attack, the attacker wins on a tie right ? Am I missing something or misunderstanding your post ?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T05:54:41-07:00","id":1381300,"title":"","content":"That's not an opposed roll, it's a Difficulty.<br /> <br /> If something is Difficulty 1, you need 1 or more. If it's Difficulty 4, you need 4 or more.<br /> When you attack someone with Parry 8, it's difficulty 8, so you need 8 or more.<br /> <br /> When both of you roll dice, the Defender wins. (Although in practice it's not always clear to me who is the Defender.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T05:58:39-07:00","id":1381302,"title":"","content":"Oh ok yeah if I remember correctly in 3e it's supposed to go to the player doing the best stunt or something like that. Thanks for the clarification anyway","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T06:24:12-07:00","id":1381305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1381096#post1381096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now I understand how the Getimian Exalted are supposed to be like Organization 13's named Nobodies from <i>Kingdom Hearts</i>. A person just spontaneously appears in the world with an entire life's worth of memories and strong magical powers... but with no real identity or place within the world, as far as the world is concerned.</div> </div> </div> </div>My first thought was the Four Monarchs from <i>Feng Shui</i>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> They once ruled the world as magical god-kings until their enemies changed history around them and they woke up to find themselves in an entirely different 1980's, still with some of their power, but with nobody knowing who they were and the world working entirely differently around them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2160-elemental","name":"Elemental","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2160_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"412"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T11:13:00-07:00","id":1381379,"title":"","content":"I have to wonder if the Getimians are at all related to Yatani\u2019s Children.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T11:53:31-07:00","id":1381386,"title":"","content":"You know how certain fantasies go absolutely mind-screw crazy with making clones and alternate versions of certain characters? Especially when the author actually does mean to play with the concept of self-hood and identity?<br /> <br /> It should be possible to clone a Solar Exalt with a sorcerous working. The clone won't have the Solar's Exaltation, but they could have all of the same memories and virtues and Intimacies and skills.<br /> <br /> That's not enough to earn their own Solar Exaltation... but they could receive one. Or they could receive an Abyssal Exaltation, or a Lunar Exaltation. Or maybe the original were born to a Dragon-Blooded lineage, so the clone succeeds at Terrestrial Exaltation where the original failed.<br /> <br /> Or they could have been born a clone as part of Heaven's plan for destiny, and be Chosen as a Sidereal. Or Heaven could snuff out their destiny before their birth ever started, and then one day there's a Getimian Exalt running around claiming to be your clone!<br /> <br /> Or the clone could be considered a failure, and instilled with horrible shame and treated horribly, only to receive an Infernal Exaltation.<br /> <br /> Or the clone could not be erased from the future, and yet simply... not work. The process was flawed, so the body would be still-born. Except the Dark Mother breathes into it and births a Liminal Exalt.<br /> <br /> <br /> Attempting to clone a Dragon-Blood is the only case where you might actually have decent odds of the clone getting the same Exaltation as the genetic donor. Since the clone is basically your twin.<br /> <br /> Of course, a clone who fails to receive a Terrestrial Exaltation could end up with any of the others. It certainly sets up the &quot;failed clone becomes an Infernal&quot; plot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T12:42:00-07:00","id":1381406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1381386#post1381386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It should be possible to clone a Solar Exalt with a sorcerous working.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or the craft charm where you make a clone.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The clone won't have the Solar's Exaltation, but they could have all of the same memories and virtues and Intimacies and skills.<br /> <br /> That's not enough to earn their own Solar Exaltation... but they could receive... a Lunar Exaltation. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, played that character.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T12:57:36-07:00","id":1381409,"title":"","content":"The descriptions of Getimians as people who mattered and made a heroic difference in &quot;their worlds&quot; seems to suggest some potential for parallels and contrasts against the theme of past lives of Celestial Exalted, and also the same against the narrative worlds of the Fair Folk (but with a key difference, for one, that those Fae worlds are lies and stories!).<br /> <br /> I also wonder if they'll have a Lore background that kind of reflects &quot;Things that are known commonly where I 'come from', but aren't around these parts&quot; (which seems like something which could both be true and have an monkey-paw kind of version of it). This may be a horrible idea. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2160-elemental\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2160_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2160\" data-vbnamecard=\"2160\">Elemental</a>, great reference.<br /> <br /> (I also find the idea pretty evocative of 'Great Work of Time', though not in the specific sense of characters coming from divergent continua, but in any rate that is pretty cool for Sidereals).<br /> <br /> (Thus ceases my bit of distracting from &quot;Exalted Essence Dev Interview&quot; thread to &quot;Random Getimian speculation&quot;).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T13:03:55-07:00","id":1381411,"title":"","content":"Well, as they have powers about imposing their world on Creation, some of that could be based around Establish a Fact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T13:10:46-07:00","id":1381413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1381411#post1381411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, as they have powers about imposing their world on Creation, some of that could be based around Establish a Fact.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder how effectively they can recreate their relationships and influence in the real world.<br /> <br /> &quot;I knew you in my world, and you loved me. So I find it easier to Instill in you the Intimacy that you had for me in the world that never happened.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I had children in my world. They now exist here.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T13:15:00-07:00","id":1381416,"title":"","content":"Probably depends on their essence and experience.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T13:32:48-07:00","id":1381423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1381411#post1381411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, as they have powers about imposing their world on Creation, some of that could be based around Establish a Fact.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kind of. I'm talking about things which are already true in both worlds, but not a lot of people know them in Creation-Creation, but they are generally known in alternate-Creation (&quot;The father of the Satrap's illegitimate daughter is....&quot;, the legend of how &quot;The 5 Thieves had to do X, Y and Z to access the secret room in Jashua the Solar's Tomb&quot;, where no one in Creation-Creation knows it exists, etc.). Not imposing the reality and truths of their Creation, which aren't true in Creation-Creation, on Creation-Creation. Though that is cool also.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T14:05:39-07:00","id":1381432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1381386#post1381386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.<br /> <br /> <br /> Attempting to clone a Dragon-Blood is the only case where you might actually have decent odds of the clone getting the same Exaltation as the genetic donor. Since the clone is basically your twin.<br /> <br /> Of course, a clone who fails to receive a Terrestrial Exaltation could end up with any of the others. It certainly sets up the &amp;quot;failed clone becomes an Infernal&amp;quot; plot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on the diners age, even if the clone is newly created. If it comes up with the same maturity and memories of the Dragon-Blooded, I can see it already being past the age cap","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T14:06:02-07:00","id":1381433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1381413#post1381413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder how effectively they can recreate their relationships and influence in the real world.<br /> <br /> &quot;I knew you in my world, and you loved me. So I find it easier to Instill in you the Intimacy that you had for me in the world that never happened.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I saw that specifically mentioned as a charm they had, on the Discord server.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/91-wandering","name":"Wandering","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar91_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T18:53:18-07:00","id":1381499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1381413#post1381413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder how effectively they can recreate their relationships and influence in the real world.<br /> <br /> &quot;I knew you in my world, and you loved me. So I find it easier to Instill in you the Intimacy that you had for me in the world that never happened.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that's a Charm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;I had children in my world. They now exist here.&quot; </div> </div> </div>That probably will not be, if for no other reason than it's poison for pathos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T20:30:06-07:00","id":1381517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1381499#post1381499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, that's a Charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Easy call, really.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That probably will not be, if for no other reason than it's poison for pathos. </div> </div> </div>Makes sense.<br /> <br /> How possible is it that multiple Getimians are born from the same rejected future?<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, it's just cool that the &quot;I reject your reality and substitute my own!&quot; Exalted really did come from a different reality, even if it operated according to the exact same rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T04:59:35-07:00","id":1381607,"title":"","content":"The rejected world doesn\u2019t exist. Each Getemian\u2019s experience differs only by their existence as plucked from the loom of fate. That said, I guess you could have two threads cut at the same time for a Getemian pair.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my RPG podcast: <a href=\"http://thestorytold.libsyn.com\" target=\"_blank\">The Story Told</a><br /> Follow my ongoing Exalted Campaign: <a href=\"https://thefallofjiara.obsidianportal.com/adventure-log\" target=\"_blank\">The Fall of Jiara</a><br /> Check out my Community Content: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Chazz%20Kellner\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....hazz%20Kellner</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/702-elfspeaker","name":"ElfSpeaker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar702_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T09:51:49-07:00","id":1381670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElfSpeaker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1381607#post1381607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The rejected world doesn\u2019t exist. Each Getemian\u2019s experience differs only by their existence as plucked from the loom of fate. That said, I guess you could have two threads cut at the same time for a Getemian pair.</div> </div> </div> </div>The point of divergence could go a bit beyond just the Getimian's brith. The example in <i>The Realm</i> of Chanos Tsunbal, where his Great House stopped exisiting centuries ago. He seems to have been important to it though. But in any case, there's some wiggle-room to things. For some characters it'll probably be as simple as thier never having been born and the consequences. For others, it's an event centuries ago that the butterflu effect undid not just their whole life, but also those of the people and things they loved and care for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T10:00:57-07:00","id":1381674,"title":"","content":"I wonder if the basic effect of Devil body the same in Essence or somewhat simplified. \u201cBigger and more effient charms\u201d is cool, but removing Supernal means front loading a lot more effects I\u2019d imagine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T12:40:14-07:00","id":1381743,"title":"","content":"I suspect that it'll be less &quot;more efficient charms&quot; and more &quot;bigger, flashier, more demonic powers&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T12:43:37-07:00","id":1381745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1381743#post1381743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suspect that it'll be less &amp;quot;more efficient charms&amp;quot; and more &amp;quot;bigger, flashier, more demonic powers&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Likely it will be like Resonant evocations where the Charms have a note at the end that says \u201cIn Godbody [insert additional cool effect, or make the Charm free, or whatever]\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T12:57:52-07:00","id":1381748,"title":"","content":"Oh, sure.<br /> <br /> I assume it'll be a Mode, essentially (plus maybe some base benefits from the Devil-Body, like more soak or something).<br /> <br /> I started playing a Kindred of the East game recently, so several PCs have Devil-Bodies. Mine has 3 extra health levels from being 8 foot tall. Dunno what the rest have, probably Claws, that kind of thing. And they all gives us +1 Strength, Dexterity and Stamina.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-16T23:56:49-07:00","id":1382072,"title":"","content":"I will say that, while the Devil Body sounds cool, I hope they\u2019re keeping in mind the issues that DBT had in previous editions. And, if the Devil Body is supposed to be the Infernal counterpart to Supernal, I hope it can boost things aside from combat. I mean, granted, with FF7R just coming out, having an excuse to hit the One Winged Angel track during combat is very cool, but I\u2019m hoping there\u2019s room for ninjas made of cutting wind, angelic beings of inhuman perfection, and mandalas of energy that can craft anything with their minds. Stuff that has some non-combat uses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-16T23:59:51-07:00","id":1382073,"title":"","content":"So, I finally got to listen to the podcast and I wanted to ask: the discussion of difficulty and what getting 15 successes on a roll means and the whole \u201cconsequences of success\u201d thing... Are you guys gonna include some of that in Crucible of Legends too? Because I think it belongs in there too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-17T00:27:32-07:00","id":1382077,"title":"","content":"As for why there\u2019s a dedicated group of Exalted Crafter enthusiasts, I\u2019ve got my take on the reason. It might not hold for everyone. I\u2019m not even entirely sure it holds for me, but...<br /> <br /> Anyway. One of the things about the old Storyteller system is that it has a bunch of attributes and abilities. And, when you\u2019re new to the game, all of the attributes SEEM equally important, and the same for abilities. There\u2019s nothing in the rules or on the sheet that says Dexterity is twice as important as Strength or that Wits is basically never rolled or anything. It all costs the same.<br /> <br /> This creates an implied promise that you can create a character who is really in to any of these abilities and said character will be viable. And, just because the game lines usually fell down on these promises, doesn\u2019t mean that they didn\u2019t attract people who wanted to believe them.<br /> <br /> And then Exalted comes along and turns up the volume on this implied promise. \u201cLook\u201d it says \u201cwe have a class that is all about traveling around and doing paperwork and we have a bunch of magic powers that you can only get because you\u2019re so awesome at doing said paperwork! You can totally make that Ninja Accountant you\u2019ve secretly been yearning to play, it\u2019ll be awesome! Or, hey, you can be a legendary Blacksmith that makes stuff like Kusenagi or Excalibur, how does that sound?\u201d<br /> <br /> And, just because the game didn\u2019t fully execute on this promise, didn\u2019t mean people didn\u2019t want to buy into it. <br /> <br /> Personally, I\u2019m of the right age where all I really want from an RPG is to be able to play MacGyver. Someone who can use Science and Technology to quickly Craft a solution to any problem that might be at hand. And, while Exalted isn\u2019t necessarily the best fit for that character, I had great fun with a mortal Thaumaturge in a 2e game who quickly mixed up a potion to drop a tree on the spirit we were fighting at the time. And stuff like Craftsman Needs No Tools is perfect for this type of person, even if the rules aren\u2019t really set up for mortal level crafts to matter very much.<br /> <br /> Point is that, Exalted promised me a long time ago that I could make a cool craftsperson and, despite the various issues over the years, I think 3e has mostly succeeded in that area (not that improvements couldn\u2019t be had). And I\u2019d just be sad if Essence backed off from that. Plus, if you dropped that from the game, why even bother with the Twilight Caste?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-17T00:39:17-07:00","id":1382082,"title":"","content":"Certainly I have found that dedicated Crafters do turn up fairly often. It's something very few other games do much with, so it stands out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-17T00:53:22-07:00","id":1382085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1382077#post1382077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for why there\u2019s a dedicated group of Exalted Crafter enthusiasts, I\u2019ve got my take on the reason. It might not hold for everyone. I\u2019m not even entirely sure it holds for me, but...<br /> <br /> Anyway. One of the things about the old Storyteller system is that it has a bunch of attributes and abilities. And, when you\u2019re new to the game, all of the attributes SEEM equally important, and the same for abilities. There\u2019s nothing in the rules or on the sheet that says Dexterity is twice as important as Strength or that Wits is basically never rolled or anything. It all costs the same.<br /> <br /> This creates an implied promise that you can create a character who is really in to any of these abilities and said character will be viable. And, just because the game lines usually fell down on these promises, doesn\u2019t mean that they didn\u2019t attract people who wanted to believe them.<br /> <br /> And then Exalted comes along and turns up the volume on this implied promise. \u201cLook\u201d it says \u201cwe have a class that is all about traveling around and doing paperwork and we have a bunch of magic powers that you can only get because you\u2019re so awesome at doing said paperwork! You can totally make that Ninja Accountant you\u2019ve secretly been yearning to play, it\u2019ll be awesome! Or, hey, you can be a legendary Blacksmith that makes stuff like Kusenagi or Excalibur, how does that sound?\u201d<br /> <br /> And, just because the game didn\u2019t fully execute on this promise, didn\u2019t mean people didn\u2019t want to buy into it.<br /> <br /> Personally, I\u2019m of the right age where all I really want from an RPG is to be able to play MacGyver. Someone who can use Science and Technology to quickly Craft a solution to any problem that might be at hand. And, while Exalted isn\u2019t necessarily the best fit for that character, I had great fun with a mortal Thaumaturge in a 2e game who quickly mixed up a potion to drop a tree on the spirit we were fighting at the time. And stuff like Craftsman Needs No Tools is perfect for this type of person, even if the rules aren\u2019t really set up for mortal level crafts to matter very much.<br /> <br /> Point is that, Exalted promised me a long time ago that I could make a cool craftsperson and, despite the various issues over the years, I think 3e has mostly succeeded in that area (not that improvements couldn\u2019t be had). And I\u2019d just be sad if Essence backed off from that. Plus, if you dropped that from the game, why even bother with the Twilight Caste?</div> </div> </div> </div>I like how Craftsman Needs No Tools allow for very cool stunts in social/action scene where you can craft instantly anything that makes your action cooler, but is not necessary (breathing a present out of an uncut gem, etc ...). I find it very cool","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-17T00:58:23-07:00","id":1382086,"title":"","content":"Finally got a chance to listen to it. I wonder how/if the further flattening of the power curve is going to affect the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-17T03:28:41-07:00","id":1382107,"title":"","content":"Tbh, I don't think it'll affect the setting at all.<br /> <br /> The setting, being a fictional creation, is somewhat independent of the rules. It's just that the more it seems at-odds with the rules, the less it has versimilitude. But it's not like you can run a simulation of &quot;with this disparity of power level, what does Creation look like&quot;.<br /> <br /> However, previously in 2nd ed, people often complained that the Lunar Elders and Deathlords were far too powerful rules-wise for what they seemed to do in-setting, and others to a lesser extent.<br /> <br /> 3rd ed flattened this a bit (Raksi, Ma-Ha-Suchi, etc, are much less powerful than in 2nd ed, and I know the intention was for Deathlords to be significantly less powerful. Certainly the Silver Prince's short write-up doesn't make him sound very powerful). This gives it a bit more versimillitude, because you don't have to ask &quot;why doesn't FaFL just kill everyone with his Creation-Slaying Oblivion Kick&quot; or whatever.<br /> <br /> If Essence flattens it a bit more, then I don't think anyone reading the setting would notice unless they'd already convinced themselves that the rules=fluff in a way that makes perfect sense. But as I said, there's not really a way to test it.<br /> <br /> Certainly, I haven't got the impression that they intend to rewrite the setting significantly... though I do think Neall mentioned that they might change the way it's presented slightly to emphasise the disparity of power level less?<br /> (Tbh, I always felt the setting presented the Solars as a bit too powerful, considering the average Solar is way less experienced than the average Dragonblood or Lunar. But I guess 2nd ed combat Solars were truly ridiculous in practice.)<br /> My impression was that this was more about encouraging mixed-play than changing the setting per-se, but I could be wrong.<br /> <br /> Now, saying that, if the power level between Dragonblood and Solars/Abyssals/Infernals is compressed<i> too</i> much, then you may ask why 300 Exalts are a threat to 20,000 Exalts.<br /> <br /> For PCs, it's not an issue really of course; if all the PCs are Solars they'll get xp at such a ridiculous rate compared to NPCs that they'll still be able to challenge Dragonblood who are much older than them. But I imagine that there'll be a lot more mixed groups with 10 options! (Which, considering how few Solars are in the world, I mean it's like 40 in the Scavenger Lands, 20 in the West, 30 in the North... really not many.) So that doesn't really work.<br /> <br /> (My 1600-year old Lunar elder flipped out and screamed for several minutes last session when he discovered his new Solar friend knew Solar sorcery despite only being about 80. F***ing Solars and their ridiculous XP gain.)<br /> <br /> I also wondered whether, with Dragonblood, they'll somehow fluff it in to explain the lack of disparity.<br /> What I mean is, in 3rd edition, Solars get 46 motes and 15 charms after a few months to a year since exaltation. That's far, far more than a Dragonblood who's been exalted for that amount of time.<br /> But of course, unless you're doing a high-school game, you don't play Dragonblood who've been exalted for a few months, you play Dragonblood after about 10-20 years since exaltation; and you get 44 motes and 15 charms.<br /> <br /> So maybe all PCs will start with Essence 1, 5 motes, 10 charms, or however it'll work with Essence, and their charms will be largely of a similar level (with Solars getting some slightly stronger effects, plus the free excellencies, but of course they're social outcasts rather than being seen as living bodhisvatta-nobles), but it's not actually supposed to represent a similar Solar, Lunar and Dragonblood, but rather a 3-month Solar, 1-year Lunar and 20-years-since-exaltation Dragonblood.<br /> <br /> So when you fight Wyld Hunt Shikari or experienced Dragonblood legion officers... they're basically little more than starting characters. Whereas a Lunar NPC of the same age has much better stats than a starting character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 04-17-2020, 06:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-17T04:39:23-07:00","id":1382120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1382107#post1382107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(with Solars getting some slightly stronger effects, plus the free excellencies, but of course they're social outcasts rather than being seen as living bodhisvatta-nobles)</div> </div> </div> </div> Do we know what the DB Advantages are? Because this made me realize that &quot;you are a Prince of the Earth and no one dares question that&quot; would be a pretty good one.<br /> <br /> It's just an idle thought, of course. and not what I actually expect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-17T05:58:49-07:00","id":1382138,"title":"","content":"They haven't said yet.<br /> <br /> I was thinking about that, and I guessed maybe one would be Anima Flux. The other I'm not sure. Could be something to do with Sworn Kin. Could be a social benefit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-17T07:29:10-07:00","id":1382157,"title":"","content":"Given people's suggestions about how to represent therianthrophy (animal metamorphosis), I wonder if the Lunar ability to assume other human faces won't be their second Advantage. If only to keep the word-count small and simple in regards to their first Advantage.<br /> <br /> The Solar Bond could be the second Advantage, but it's not quite universal enough since not every Lunar character will be in a group with a Solar, let alone their Solar Mate.<br /> <br /> <br /> I wouldn't worry too much about the power-curve between Terrestrials and Solars flattening and how it might affect the setting.<br /> <br /> The Solars of the First Age were such a threat because they had grown so much OLDER than Terrestrials, and because they controlled a society built to serve them, including legions of Terrestrials still loyal to them.<br /> <br /> Plus, those Solars didn't merely control Artifacts they themselves had made, but also Artifacts their kingdoms of servants had made for them, and vast infrastructure fashioned collectively by the entire Exalted Host working together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-17T08:19:26-07:00","id":1382165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1382157#post1382157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Solar Bond could be the second Advantage, but it's not quite universal enough since not every Lunar character will be in a group with a Solar, let alone their Solar Mate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that Heirs is adding the possibility for DBs to become Solar Mates, Essence might go further and let you take any other non-Lunar as your Solar Mate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-17T14:00:26-07:00","id":1382237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1382107#post1382107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, saying that, if the power level between Dragonblood and Solars/Abyssals/Infernals is compressed<i> too</i> much, then you may ask why 300 Exalts are a threat to 20,000 Exalts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, this is one issue I see maybe cropping up. There's 20,000 DBs, if 300 new DBs arose with sun powers instead of elemental powers, it wouldn't really rock the boat very much. That being said, I'm really not at all a big fan of the Solars are back, so it's only a matter of days before one of them casually knocks over the entire Dragonblooded hegemony and then past that maybe a matter of weeks before they all take over the Lunar dominions as well. Then the Abyssals, Infernals and Solars can duke it out over Creation using the other exalted as pawns.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1382107#post1382107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solars getting some slightly stronger effects, plus the free excellencies, but of course they're social outcasts rather than being seen as living bodhisvatta-nobles</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that it may be necessary to walk back a bit how much the Solars are hunted by the Realm and defined as demons by the nearly global religion. Then again I've seen a lot of new players either shy away from Solars because of that, or just not really get how bad that can be. Maybe if they ease up on the Anathema thing a lot, but it would definitely feel different to be a Solar then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-17T14:21:13-07:00","id":1382241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now, saying that, if the power level between Dragonblood and Solars/Abyssals/Infernals is compressed<i> too</i> much, then you may ask why 300 Exalts are a threat to 20,000 Exalts. </div> </div> </div>I mean, even if the Charms are less powerful, the simple fact that there exist Celestial and Solar Sorcery (if it still exists in some form or another in Essence) is enough to make The Realm scared about the return of the Solar, they don't need to crush The Realm easily with 300 vs 20 000, they just need to have tools at their disposal that are scary enough that the threat can look serious","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-17T14:32:55-07:00","id":1382246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1382241#post1382241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, even if the Charms are less powerful, the simple fact that there exist Celestial and Solar Sorcery (if it still exists in some form or another in Essence) is enough to make The Realm scared about the return of the Solar, they don't need to crush The Realm easily with 300 vs 20 000, they just need to have tools at their disposal that are scary enough that the threat can look serious</div> </div> </div> </div>There's also the worry that the Solars will find hidden Doomsday Devices left behind by their predecessors that no one else could find or use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-17T14:32:55-07:00","id":1382247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1382241#post1382241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, even if the Charms are less powerful, the simple fact that there exist Celestial and Solar Sorcery (if it still exists in some form or another in Essence) is enough to make The Realm scared about the return of the Solar, they don't need to crush The Realm easily with 300 vs 20 000, they just need to have tools at their disposal that are scary enough that the threat can look serious</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine the Sorcery Levels are still a Thing. Like, Solars no longer being able to Roflstomp 20-100 Dragon Bloods doesn't mean they're not still dangerous and in a position to make the existing status quo <i>very messy.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-17T14:33:21-07:00","id":1382248,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't want Solar players (who've likely picked Solars because they wanted to be powerful-but-young heroes) to feel like they definitely should take sorcery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-17T14:42:27-07:00","id":1382250,"title":"","content":"Also the eternal thing that since you can't stop the new solars from coming into existence the new count would be worrisome on the grounds of it being the same problem as the lunars. And the concern that the solars might eventually start making some organization like the Silver Pact. Even if the Realm collectively believed and were correct in assuming that the Solars, Abyssals, and Inferals weren't any more dangerous to itself than the Lunars I can't imagine it would be very happy to have another front to war on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-17T15:13:00-07:00","id":1382254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1382138#post1382138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was thinking about that, and I guessed maybe one would be Anima Flux. The other I'm not sure. Could be something to do with Sworn Kin. Could be a social benefit.</div> </div> </div> </div> Anima Flux and Kinships feel most likely, but a man can dream.<br /> <br /> Anima Flux <i>could</i> be made part of the individual Aspects' anima powers, since they've always had Aspect-dependent riders anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1382237#post1382237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that it may be necessary to walk back a bit how much the Solars are hunted by the Realm and defined as demons by the nearly global religion. Then again I've seen a lot of new players either shy away from Solars because of that, or just not really get how bad that can be. Maybe if they ease up on the Anathema thing a lot, but it would definitely feel different to be a Solar then.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'd argue that having to limit your power to avoid being hunted is kind of a core Solar experience. Hell, I'm fairly certain it's one of the reasons animas exist in the game. If anything, it's an aspect of the game that should be emphasized, so that players don't come in with the assumption that they can just burn Essence without consequence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-17T15:37:09-07:00","id":1382258,"title":"","content":"Ultimately, y'know, we talk about power levels a lot, but as long as it feels meaningful and strong for Solars to be &quot;the best&quot;, and we're willing to compromise on how that's realized and be friendly to allowing it to work, there's lots of room for that to work, under whatever &quot;the gap&quot; is. <br /> <br /> (Slight Tangent: Totally not about anyone in this dialogue at the moment, but there is a sometimes a tendency to just fixate on the raw size of the Terrestrial and Solar host, and then set us up a criteria where, if a Solar standing on a featureless plain can't handle 100x the amount of Dragonblooded, then the system is somehow failing. And if you set that challenge up, then the system is doomed to fail one way or the other - because it either meet that criteria and then fails to evoke all that it suggests in setting text about how Solars and DBs &quot;throw down&quot; (which sure as hell ain't 100:1!), or if just fails to meet that criteria directly.<br /> <br /> I think that we have to accept a fairly flexible idea of Solar greatness where they do have to tactically apply that greatness and rely on external factors in the world to amplify the effect of their skill, and it's not simply a matter of, y'know, this sort of &quot;In any situation, an individual Solar must be (total DB host:total Solar host ratio) more powerful, purely through internal power&quot;, which is an goal that is just setting things up to fail.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-18T14:08:00-07:00","id":1382381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1382258#post1382258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ultimately, y'know, we talk about power levels a lot, but as long as it feels meaningful and strong for Solars to be &quot;the best&quot;, and we're willing to compromise on how that's realized and be friendly to allowing it to work, there's lots of room for that to work, under whatever &quot;the gap&quot; is.<br /> <br /> (Slight Tangent: Totally not about anyone in this dialogue at the moment, but there is a sometimes a tendency to just fixate on the raw size of the Terrestrial and Solar host, and then set us up a criteria where, if a Solar standing on a featureless plain can't handle 100x the amount of Dragonblooded, then the system is somehow failing. And if you set that challenge up, then the system is doomed to fail one way or the other - because it either meet that criteria and then fails to evoke all that it suggests in setting text about how Solars and DBs &quot;throw down&quot; (which sure as hell ain't 100:1!), or if just fails to meet that criteria directly.<br /> <br /> I think that we have to accept a fairly flexible idea of Solar greatness where they do have to tactically apply that greatness and rely on external factors in the world to amplify the effect of their skill, and it's not simply a matter of, y'know, this sort of &quot;In any situation, an individual Solar must be (total DB host:total Solar host ratio) more powerful, purely through internal power&quot;, which is an goal that is just setting things up to fail.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Plus...Exalted is not D&amp;D. D&amp;D is built such that each class has a spot on the combat power curve and, as they go up in level, they will automatically go up that power curve. Thus you can say things like \u201ca 15th level character will always beat a 5th level character\u201d and have them be more or less true. <br /> <br /> Exalted is a game where a given character\u2019s competencies are only roughly set by their exalt type and caste. You can build a chargen Dawn that can wreck face to the point that only some of the more powerful demons in the core might be legit challenges for them... or you can build a pacifist solar doctor who couldn\u2019t fight their way out of a paper bag, but can cure plagues, cancer, and so on.<br /> <br /> So, the power curve discussion in Exalted doesn\u2019t necessarily bear out in play all the time, because unless you\u2019re on the extreme ends, there\u2019s always someone more powerful than you, even if they should be \u201cweaker.\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T04:25:42-07:00","id":1382492,"title":"","content":"I am going to go against the consensus here, and hope that they increase the disparity between Solars and DB in Essence. Increase it in favor of the Solars, I mean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12357-marcob","name":"Marcob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12357_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T04:36:53-07:00","id":1382494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1382492#post1382492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am going to go against the consensus here, and hope that they increase the disparity between Solars and DB in Essence. Increase it in favor of the Solars, I mean.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I'm fine both ways. I've said this numerous times, but what will make the most important success of effectively representing some Exalted being stronger than others, is making good antagonists rules. I'm absolutely sure that, whatever the quality of the PC's design may be, if the Antagonist's section and the ST tools do not follow adequately in term of design, people will have exactly the same problems they already have with Exalted 3e Core, albeit with simpler rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T05:06:31-07:00","id":1382496,"title":"","content":"A very good point Chausse.<br /> <br /> Frankly, the NPC Exalted in the Core are all quite weak, so if you're a hearth of DBs the Abyssals and Lunars are easy to beat and if you're a group of Solars the DBs are easy to beat (despite being essence 2 or 3).<br /> <br /> Although that's partly because the setting says &quot;Solars are really powerful&quot; and then you've got five. Who in theory have one member who's really good at combat, and a couple who are quite good, and a couple who are not, but in practice have 3 who are really good at combat and two who are quite good.<br /> <br /> Anyway, it's fine for E1 Solars if the players aren't aiming to optimise for maximum killitude, it's just at E4 or 5 it falls apart. At least, that's my experience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 04-19-2020, 08:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T05:35:53-07:00","id":1382501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1382492#post1382492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am going to go against the consensus here, and hope that they increase the disparity between Solars and DB in Essence. Increase it in favor of the Solars, I mean.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm afraid the writers have said they aim to flatten things a bit to encourage mixed-splat play.<br /> <br /> Not saying you are wrong to want that, if that's what you enjoy, but I'm afraid you are almost certainly going to be disappointed.<br /> <br /> Of course, I don't have much idea what &quot;flattened power&quot; actually looks like in practice. Some identical charms, yes. Other charms that are similar but better, but I don't know how much better.<br /> <br /> And there is the way the Exalt advantages work: Solars get free excellencies (though excellencies are different, so don't know how good that is, but it certainly seems good... also simple as it reduces counting) and always win draws. Liminals can touch/see ghosts and come back to life if their brains aren't damaged. Sidereals are forgettable if you don't have intimacies and can fate-weave people into stereotypical roles giving them a bonus to appropriate things (eg you fate-wave them to be a baker and they can turn the Sidereal's essence x dice into successes on baking. You fate-wave them into a warrior and I assume they get the same on attacks?).<br /> <br /> So there might be a certain element of &quot;Solars roll more successes, other splats are more flexible&quot; (for example, interacting with ghosts is very easy for Liminals).<br /> So it may be that the splats are more equally<i> useful </i>in a game, but not necessarily more powerful. (Which is what I tend to find in Solar+Lunar games anyway. Solars are more powerful, yeah, but in reality the Lunars end up being just as useful to the group. Hmmm... actually in the more mixed game I play I'd say two of the Solars don't do a ton to help the others because they're focused on their own stuff, two Solars can be very useful or very problematic, the Raksha isn't very useful except in a fight, the DBs haven't done a ton, and the most useful to the group is the Lunar but she does need motivating. Essentially, while the DBs and Raksha definitely are weaker, how useful they are to the plot and group is more about the characters' personalities than their abilities.)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T05:36:54-07:00","id":1382502,"title":"","content":"One thing I do really hope, and think this is more important than flattening splats, is that they flatten the difference in power between players who know the game and character gen system really well and care about optimisation... and those that don't.<br /> <br /> And make the social system easier to understand/use for the non-rules/mechanics inclined.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T07:41:47-07:00","id":1382523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1382496#post1382496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A very good point Chausse.<br /> <br /> Frankly, the NPC Exalted in the Core are all quite weak, so if you're a hearth of DBs the Abyssals and Lunars are easy to beat and if you're a group of Solars the DBs are easy to beat (despite being essence 2 or 3).<br /> <br /> Although that's partly because the setting says &quot;Solars are really powerful&quot; and then you've got five. Who in theory have one member who's really good at combat, and a couple who are quite good, and a couple who are not, but in practice have 3 who are really good at combat and two who are quite good.<br /> <br /> Anyway, it's fine for E1 Solars if the players aren't aiming to optimise for maximum killitude, it's just at E4 or 5 it falls apart. At least, that's my experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's not only about &quot;having strong enemies that kills PC&quot;, but also about having ST tools in many different area (action, social, investigation, etc ...) that can challenge PCs. Suppose you are a ST, you just have the Core Book, and you want your enemies (probably Lunars, but maybe Dragon-Blooded or something like this) to be able to to take the control of the Senate or whatever in the country the Solars live in. You can of course always take the narratives ST approach (which I advise) : As long as your enemies got the means to do what they want, they succeed and i's going on. But if at a certain point you need to confront PC's and NPC's (Say, one Solar uses the power Bureaucracy Essence 1 to delay bureaucratic procedures and delay your villains), then what do you do ? Obviously, you can always say &quot;Well they try to find another solution&quot;, but with the Core Book, you have absolutely no tool or help to deal with this kind of situation. So either your PC's directly succeed, or you try to use some plot to make your scheme advance (villains kidnap a senator, etc ...). But at no moment the rules hep you by saying &quot;Well this kind of Exalted could have this kind of power that would challenge characters on this specific field&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":24291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","user":"Chausse","date":". 04-19-2020, 11:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T07:46:51-07:00","id":1382524,"title":"","content":"I think one thing about Essence is that it should make making your own antagonists easier. When I first ran 3rd ed, my antagonists were all mortals (who were beaten easily), 2nd circle demons, or Solars. Because that was basically all I had. The occasional DB who was beaten easily. Oh and there was an Exigent with Ahlat charms once. And looots of battle groups.<br /> <br /> Whereas with Essence a)there's 10 kinds of Exalts to choose NPCs from, b)there's rules for their social stuff, rather than just low-level combat, and c)a simpler system means making your own NPCs should be easier, especially at high levels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T12:36:36-07:00","id":1382571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1382492#post1382492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am going to go against the consensus here, and hope that they increase the disparity between Solars and DB in Essence. Increase it in favor of the Solars, I mean.</div> </div> </div> </div>Based on the descriptions on the podcast and devs elsewhere, this is pretty solidly not the route they're going.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T23:46:56-07:00","id":1382687,"title":"","content":"Aaaand... I have mixed feelings after listening to the interview.<br /> <br /> I share most of the points made by the people behind Essence, and that is exciting.<br /> <br /> But now I have lost almost all my interest for Exigents, and maybe all future exalt charmsets. If Essence does it for me, then I don't want to read any Ex3 mechanics ever again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T23:53:44-07:00","id":1382688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gonzo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1382687#post1382687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But now I have lost almost all my interest for Exigents, and maybe all future exalt charmsets. If Essence does it for me, then I don't want to read any Ex3 mechanics ever again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? Why is that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T00:05:46-07:00","id":1382689,"title":"","content":"Well, the reason I was interested in Exigents was the promise of a working guide for writing charms. This would have been useful to update Infernal, Sidereal, or Alchemical characters from Ex2 (which, let's be honest, we won't see them anytime soon).<br /> <br /> But Essence not only does not use the Ex3 mechanics, it will help me play 10 exalt types with a system I can actually enjoy. Why would I need Exigents now?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T00:13:33-07:00","id":1382690,"title":"","content":"Ah okay I misunderstood, I thought you meant you thought every exalt type past exigents was going to be done poorly with bad design goals or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T00:20:31-07:00","id":1382691,"title":"","content":"The non-Charmset parts of the books have been often some fo the more awesome. Also with 10 Exalt types, there will probably be a need to do some converting of a good chunk of things left on the cutting room floor anyhow (which there will be guides to do so in <b>Essence</b>).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T00:45:51-07:00","id":1382693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gonzo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1382689#post1382689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the reason I was interested in Exigents was the promise of a working guide for writing charms. This would have been useful to update Infernal, Sidereal, or Alchemical characters from Ex2 (which, let's be honest, we won't see them anytime soon).<br /> <br /> But Essence not only does not use the Ex3 mechanics, it will help me play 10 exalt types with a system I can actually enjoy. Why would I need Exigents now?</div> </div> </div> </div>this is completely fair but also nails an issue I\u2019m mildly concerned about - that by having two ongoing editions of Exalted, OPP will end up co petting with itself. I suppose the goal would be after the Essence core for future supplements to include both 3e and Essence mechanics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T01:14:58-07:00","id":1382694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1382693#post1382693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> this is completely fair but also nails an issue I\u2019m mildly concerned about - that by having two ongoing editions of Exalted, OPP will end up co petting with itself. I suppose the goal would be after the Essence core for future supplements to include both 3e and Essence mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>What would the supplements even be? Essence will have all ten Exalted full right out of the gate, and every system detailed. If you want fluff supplements you can grab anything from any edition and use it.<br /> <br /> I like that Essence exists, but I don\u2019t think my group will be playing it. I like the tactical decision making involved in it, and a lot of the big cool charm cascades. Although I\u2019m totally open to changing my mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T02:06:31-07:00","id":1382698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1382693#post1382693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> this is completely fair but also nails an issue I\u2019m mildly concerned about - that by having two ongoing editions of Exalted, OPP will end up co petting with itself. I suppose the goal would be after the Essence core for future supplements to include both 3e and Essence mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering that Essence doesn't seem to be including more than the minimum amount of setting detail necessary to tell the stories of the various exalts it wouldn't make sense to just grab Essence, you'd most definitely want books like The Realm, Across the Eight Directions and other setting books since you'd need them to tell the story, and likely Crucible for the same reason. <i>Hypothetically </i>this could but them at odds with splat books like What Fire has Wrought and Fangs at the Gate, but I'd still want those to get a better idea of what stories to tell of the various splats and what role they have in the greater setting, I doubt for example that Essence will have more than a page on the Silver Pact compared to the extensive detail the Lunars book will have. Likewise most unique charms probably won't make it into Essence, but I've seen it mentioned that it wouldn't be too hard to convert them so you'd still want to pick up the splat for their mechanics to loot if nothing else.<br /> <br /> It was mentioned that Essence isn't 3e-2, just an alternate system you could use to play the existing 3e exalted, so this would both act as a good way to attract players driven off by the system's minutiae (including my group, half of ours didn't like the system and the other half, including myself, wanted to wait for more exalt splats, and our newer players would <i>definitely</i> be intimidated), and act as a gateway for new players who might be intimidated by the system but may want to move to core after a few months of playing.<br /> <br /> At worst, and assuming everyone would get the books, the players would want have Essence and maybe their preferred splat, and the Storyteller would want the setting books and relevant splats, depending on how the group shares the books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3729,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","user":"Darkfoxdev","date":". 04-20-2020, 05:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","name":"Darkfoxdev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T03:50:08-07:00","id":1382707,"title":"","content":"Hmmm... If they do a Sorcery book maybe it'll have rules for converting to Essence. And I guess an Essence bestiary would be possible (though if it's simple enough that may not be necessary). But no, generally, I can't see a need for new mechanics books to include Essence rules, because when Sidereals comes out Essence will already be out with rules for Sidereals, etc.<br /> <br /> In terms of competition, I guess the hope is that loads of people who are put off by Exalted's rules will start playing Essence, and this will help Across the Eight Directions and the Realm sell better, and to a lesser extent the splat and extension books.<br /> <br /> Certainly, while I am reasonably happy to play/run Exalted with my friends who have played it for a decade, I've never tried introducing it to my DnD group, unlike Vampire/Mage/Star Ears: Edge of the Empire. But a much simpler system would tempt me to try.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T05:01:36-07:00","id":1382715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1382492#post1382492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am going to go against the consensus here, and hope that they increase the disparity between Solars and DB in Essence. Increase it in favor of the Solars, I mean.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why? For what reason?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T05:10:02-07:00","id":1382716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1382715#post1382715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why? For what reason?</div> </div> </div> </div>If I may answer for myself : I like the idea of the Celestials being on a different levels than the Terrestrials. I like how the Dragon-Blooded couldn't keep the magic of the world created by the Celestials, and that only the Celestials have the power to make Creation shine in glory. The depictions of how the world was most likely doomed without the sheer power of Solars really stayed in my imagination, and I'm interested in them being on a different power level. (and of course other compete with other Celestials as well)<br /> <br /> I'm not saying I want Essence to reflect this specific aspect of the setting at all cost, but I sure would be interested to see it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T07:45:40-07:00","id":1382752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1382715#post1382715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why? For what reason?</div> </div> </div> </div>Chausse answered it perfectly.<br /> <br /> The idea that Solars are far above DB in power has stuck with me ever since I started playing Exalted. One of my eternal criticisms about 3E is that it lowered the ceiling a great deal and brought Solars and DB closer together in terms of power level. I understand why it was done, ie multi-splat parties, but I still feel like it was a mistake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12357-marcob","name":"Marcob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12357_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T07:57:44-07:00","id":1382755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1382752#post1382752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Chausse answered it perfectly.<br /> <br /> The idea that Solars are far above DB in power has stuck with me ever since I started playing Exalted. One of my eternal criticisms about 3E is that it lowered the ceiling a great deal and brought Solars and DB closer together in terms of power level. I understand why it was done, ie multi-splat parties, but I still feel like it was a mistake.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally what I like in 3e is that Solars can still do wonders DB can only dream about (Celestial+ sorcery, Craft Artefacts 5+, and many Charms). I've not played former editions, so I didn't have expectations coming in Exalted 3e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T08:00:41-07:00","id":1382756,"title":"","content":"I'm going to put on my Exalted fan hat rather than speaking as a podcast or member of the team. To me, the difference in power was always more about the extent of what Solars could create in terms of artifice and sorcery rather than the pure dice count or raw power of charms. It also accounted for the place at the pinnacle of Creation's hierarchy and the favor of the gods. Any individual Solar (or generally the celestial Exalted) don't need to be more powerful or divided into clear tiers of power for that to remain narrative true.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my RPG podcast: <a href=\"http://thestorytold.libsyn.com\" target=\"_blank\">The Story Told</a><br /> Follow my ongoing Exalted Campaign: <a href=\"https://thefallofjiara.obsidianportal.com/adventure-log\" target=\"_blank\">The Fall of Jiara</a><br /> Check out my Community Content: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Chazz%20Kellner\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....hazz%20Kellner</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/702-elfspeaker","name":"ElfSpeaker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar702_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T08:03:08-07:00","id":1382759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1382755#post1382755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Personally what I like in 3e is that Solars can still do wonders DB can only dream about (Celestial+ sorcery, Craft Artefacts 5+, and many Charms). I've not played former editions, so I didn't have expectations coming in Exalted 3e.</div> </div> </div> </div>I started in 2E and liked the edition despite its flaws, which is anathema around here, appropriately enough. That incarnation of the system really sold the power level difference between the Celestials and the Dragonblooded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12357-marcob","name":"Marcob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12357_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T08:18:26-07:00","id":1382761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1382759#post1382759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I started in 2E and liked the edition despite its flaws, which is anathema around here, appropriately enough. That incarnation of the system really sold the power level difference between the Celestials and the Dragonblooded.</div> </div> </div> </div>Didn't play it as I said, but from what I've seen there seems to be a lot of stuff about Perfect Defenses etc ... that really put different beings in totally different tiers of play.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/702-elfspeaker\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar702_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"702\" data-vbnamecard=\"702\">ElfSpeaker</a> That's what I meant when I said I liked the fact that Solars had access to Solar Sorcery, Craft, etc ... That really emphasizes why the DB couldn't maintain The First Age.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T08:35:27-07:00","id":1382764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1382693#post1382693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> this is completely fair but also nails an issue I\u2019m mildly concerned about - that by having two ongoing editions of Exalted, OPP will end up co petting with itself. I suppose the goal would be after the Essence core for future supplements to include both 3e and Essence mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think overall Ex3 needs Exalted Essence because as a community we suffer from a nasty complexity addiction born out of people's attempts to fix 2nd edition.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T09:00:18-07:00","id":1382768,"title":"","content":"To address the self-competition, I think it's important to reiterate that Essence is going to be a single project, not an ongoing line. So for the setting material, there's only going to be one set of books. Additionally, Essence can be an entry point for new folks to join Exalted. That's the intention anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my RPG podcast: <a href=\"http://thestorytold.libsyn.com\" target=\"_blank\">The Story Told</a><br /> Follow my ongoing Exalted Campaign: <a href=\"https://thefallofjiara.obsidianportal.com/adventure-log\" target=\"_blank\">The Fall of Jiara</a><br /> Check out my Community Content: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Chazz%20Kellner\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....hazz%20Kellner</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/702-elfspeaker","name":"ElfSpeaker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar702_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T09:22:01-07:00","id":1382774,"title":"","content":"I reckon if it's wildly successful, they will do supplements for it (I mean, why not?), but as we already said... how much can they do? It already has the rules for 10 Exalt types. And the fluff books are the same.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T09:35:13-07:00","id":1382777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1382774#post1382774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I reckon if it's wildly successful, they will do supplements for it (I mean, why not?), but as we already said... how much can they do? It already has the rules for 10 Exalt types. And the fluff books are the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, even if it is successful. At most I can imagine is a companion book from the Kickstarter, since there has been a lot of emphasis to try to have it as a single package. I expect more material coming out of the Vault then anything else","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T09:37:45-07:00","id":1382778,"title":"","content":"A companion book from a kickstarter does seem quite plausible actually. They seem to have been successful with the others after all (though slightly less so with Moon-Faced Strangers than Heirs to the Shogunate).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T09:48:26-07:00","id":1382781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1382774#post1382774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I reckon if it's wildly successful, they will do supplements for it (I mean, why not?), but as we already said... how much can they do? It already has the rules for 10 Exalt types. And the fluff books are the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends? Is Essence going to have rules on how to create enemies from other books that are not Exalted? If yes, then there is nothing to do. If not, a 'Essence Bestiary' would not be so bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25288-shapechanger","name":"Shapechanger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25288_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T10:09:45-07:00","id":1382784,"title":"","content":"Is Essence even getting a Kickstarter?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T10:14:50-07:00","id":1382786,"title":"","content":"They are intending to do one, yes.<br /> <br /> Although I imagine it has to be approved, and they're only at redlines, so it may not have been approved by the company yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T10:45:27-07:00","id":1382796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1382774#post1382774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I reckon if it's wildly successful, they will do supplements for it (I mean, why not?), but as we already said... how much can they do? It already has the rules for 10 Exalt types. And the fluff books are the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>The book itself will point to the other hardcovers and books for more informaiton. A snoted in the KS, it's mostly mechancis. Setting material will continue to be written with Exalted as default, and a lot of the stuff on the docket is pretty much the 3e system for different splats and such. As kind of noted, beyond conversion (which the <b>Essence </b>rules are going to have some form of built-in), there's not a lot to like, <i>do</i> that necessitates something be an <b>Essence</b> supplement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T10:53:25-07:00","id":1382798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1382755#post1382755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Personally what I like in 3e is that Solars can still do wonders DB can only dream about (Celestial+ sorcery, Craft Artefacts 5+, and many Charms). I've not played former editions, so I didn't have expectations coming in Exalted 3e.</div> </div> </div> </div>In 2e from a mechanical standpoint Solars could become essentially immune to Dragonblooded attacks. Through charms like Infinite Ability Mastery, Flurrybreakers, and something called a 2/7 filter, among others. From a fluff standpoint there were things like 10,000 Dragonblooded being marched into a tomb after a Solar to slay them, and then the tomb sealed up, with the implication I think being that the Solar slew the whole army of 10,000 but then couldn't escape before he died.<br /> <br /> You can see how that might be a problem when the Scarlet Dynasty is portrayed as a villain and they only have 10,000 dragons, and not all of them are dedicated soldiers. I think it could work, but you'd need to rework the setting and be up front that. So you might have the Realm show up with 3 legions of soldiers, and the appropriate thing is for the Dawn to say &quot;Excuse me a moment.&quot; and Horizon Severing Slash all of them to death with a back hand swing before returning to her conversation with the Abyssal.<br /> <br /> Other systems/settings work like this. Godbound does it, you literally have a player resource that you can spend to just topple an empire without rolling anything. Legacy: Godsend does it even harder, no resource required you just tell the GM you want to decimate a nation and it just happens. Those systems and settings are built around that though, they don't go into great detail about the ants that are crushed beneath your feet, and they have big, rich settings filled with a thousand things that are on your level, as you move around continent-leveling forces like pawns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T11:04:32-07:00","id":1382800,"title":"","content":"Dragon-Blooded being a bit more powerful in 3e and Solars a lower cap is in aprt since the view in 3e is that you can still have Solars be strongest without it being hyperbolically so. Right now, in 3e, Solars are still the strongest Exalt. It is just that it's not done in Isekai Anime Protagonist fashion I guess is how I would describe it. You don't just get to beat DBs a priori. If they put effort into fighting you, you have to put effort into fighting back, basically.<br /> <br /> Also note that it wasn't just the dispartiy between DBs and Solars. It was a disparity of Solars and literally everyone else, to a point where it atively harmed Charm development for other Exalts as &quot;it couldn't beat Solars.&quot; A huge issue with 2e's design is that often it set Solars at the default, and other Exalts as some downgraded version of that to keep the tiers. And there were times where even if it would have been appropriate for others to match Solars, the dictate of Solars Always Win means that these were often nerfed or Solars got basically a counter-counter to make sure they kept in place. This reuslted in the pretty much universally dispised SIdereal rules, the boring Lunar rules, and the hamstrung Abyssal ones. Inferanls were better, but note that many Charms Solars got in later stuff like Ink Monkeys or the Dreams errata, were designed as counters to some things Infernals could do to overwelm Solars. Counter-counters.<br /> <br /> Keeping things in a closer span kind of just helps keep things interesting. It's not just making DBs useful for mixed groups. It's making htem actual antagonists that you might face even later on, rather htan the Exalted equivilant of kobolds. It goes in other areas too. Solars are great at MAs and artifacts and sorcery. Note that Sidereals and Getimians are better at <i>a kind</i> of MA, but htat doesn't take away Solar capability. Solars having universal Resonance with artifacts doens't mean you can't have Infernals equal with oricalchum or Dragon-Blooded wiht jade. Lunars being equal with Solars at necromancy isn't the end of the world since it's a setting conceit that Abyssals are still bst there. Solars get their hands in a lot of pies, and have total competence in universal stuff graeter than anyone else. AN dlikely have effects that are sbutly strong as hell that add up over time in <b>Essence</b> and have one snow that just throough raw numbers, tend to overwelm others.<br /> <br /> It's just that it's less &quot;I roll 21 dice every roll&quot; and more &quot;If I use my tools in combination I probably win. But I have to have the tools, and I have to use them right.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T12:11:48-07:00","id":1382804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1382715#post1382715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why? For what reason?</div> </div> </div> </div>For me a core part of the flavor of Creation is that different Exalted sit at different levels in general potency.<br /> <br /> Personally, the biggest attraction of the Dragon Blooded is that their powers are a bit weaker than the Celestial standard - its nice to stand head and shoulders above mortals, without them being as trivial as they can feel when playing a Solar; whilst still having Celestial and Solar level big bads knocking around the setting.<br /> <br /> I would think their are other ways of &quot;evening up&quot; mixed groups than an all-round equaling of the power levels (what about bonus XP or increasing the cost of charms for the more potent Exalts when in a mixed group?)<br /> Weaker Exalt types should still have plenty of cool powers appropriate for their particular themes (flying Air Aspects for ex.) to shine in their own way.<br /> <br /> Tldr I think the power differences in 3e are pretty much spot on, they needed to be brought closer than in 2e, but do need to be there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4972,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4972-hurum","user":"hurum","date":". 04-20-2020, 04:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4972-hurum","name":"hurum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T12:57:16-07:00","id":1382811,"title":"","content":"Frankly i'm not gonna miss 2e's &quot;Solars can chump everybody&quot; attitude with a heaping side of &quot;The Dragonbloods aren't even REAL Exalts if you think about it&quot;. And i'm saying this as someone who likes Solars. Most of my concepts are Solars. But i'm okay with them being amazingly good at what they do without also going so far as to make everything that isn't a Solar a chump.<br /> <br /> I don't need my Solars to be better Sidereals than Sidereals. I don't need them to be better Dragon Bloods than Dragon Bloods. I'm good with them having edges in efficacy on their own terms (We'll see how their Advantages shake out but Free Excellencies and Wins Ties sound like nice power of theirs)<br /> <br /> I'm fine with Solar Melee letting me parry a volcano erupting without slipping in &quot;This attack is unblockable to anybody who is also not a Solar&quot;. I'm okay with Sorcery and Craft being how Solars can build and maintain the miracles of the First Age. I like the universal Resonance that Solars have, for Evocations.<br /> <br /> I am not okay with other Exalts being kneecapped for the sake of Solar Supremecy. It doesn't feel like I won if a baked in mechanic on my foe is &quot;Your defenses don't work on Solars&quot;. Like yeah, if I challenge someone to a sword fight but they immediately get paralyzed because i have brown hair, that's not really a sensation that makes me feel powerful.<br /> <br /> That's how you get things like people saying &quot;Oh the Dragon Bloods aren't real Exalts&quot; or the Alchemicals book saying &quot;Well technically the Alchemicals are PRIMORDIAL Exalts, rather than Celestial or Terrestrial, but for effects that care they cound as Celestial&quot;<br /> <br /> 2e's Solar Favortism made Terrestrial a borderline dirty word and made non-Solars a joke, if less of a punchline than Dragon Bloods thinking they mattered.<br /> <br /> So yeah. Take the idea of widening the power gap again, set it on fire, and i won't cry a tear over it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T13:02:57-07:00","id":1382815,"title":"","content":"Something worth noting too is that 3e and to some extent ExEss kind of go with PC-NPC asymmetry. This is kind of important too. A DB <i>player</i> need not be much weaker than a Solar one, while NPCs need only be as powerful or weak as needed for the kind of games being run. For a group of Celestials, the DBs need to be enough a challange to be mattering, but that depends on how many you want htere to be for that. For a Dragon-Blooded, the Anathema NPC should be a credible thret, but something in the boundaries of what you try to run. ANd since NPCs need not follow PC rules to the letter, this means that from game to game, what even the power leell of an Exalt might be is probably pretty different depending on how they're constructed. Especially if (like the game kind of is decding on now and with <b>Essence</b>) go all in on QC-style write-ups for NPCS.<br /> <br /> Like, power levels really in the end are meaningless in such an environment IMHO. And there's plenty of way sot show those levels sublty (dice caps, mote pools, access to universal stuff) than to just have a lot of effects of &quot;This, but sucks&quot; that often non-Solar Charms was written for a lot of th epast editions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T13:41:43-07:00","id":1382818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1382798#post1382798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I think it could work, but you'd need to rework the setting and be up front that. So you might have the Realm show up with 3 legions of soldiers, and the appropriate thing is for the Dawn to say &quot;Excuse me a moment.&quot; and Horizon Severing Slash all of them to death with a back hand swing before returning to her conversation with the Abyssal.<br /> <br /> Other systems/settings work like this. Godbound does it, you literally have a player resource that you can spend to just topple an empire without rolling anything. Legacy: Godsend does it even harder, no resource required you just tell the GM you want to decimate a nation and it just happens. Those systems and settings are built around that though, they don't go into great detail about the ants that are crushed beneath your feet, and they have big, rich settings filled with a thousand things that are on your level, as you move around continent-leveling forces like pawns.</div> </div> </div> </div>And this is where I gesture again at my argument again that Godbound is genius because Kevin Crawford took lots of the main beats of &quot;forum-meme-Exalted&quot; and &quot;Exalted-being-cool-but-probably-veering-away-from-its-core-coherence&quot; that emerged during 1e and 2e and then built a world and system from the ground up that totally, directly leaned in to all of that, and marketed it directly to Exalted fans who'd bought into the game on that basis.<br /> <br /> As much as, without re-litigating edition drama, I think it's great (from my perspective, ideal) that Exalted got its groove back as being &quot;Kung-fu anime Sword &amp; Sorcery with personalities and politics&quot; (there are better descriptions, but that's fairly succinct and hopefully not too horrible).<br /> <br /> ....<br /> <br /> Perhaps more constructive and useful comment for conversation : I would kind of expect it to make sense for a mechanically more simple implementation of Exalted to lean in to cross-splat play. Seems like a relative strength of a simple system? <br /> <br /> That is, it seems like in big, full mainline Exalted, it's often probably too much to handle for an ST to manage a group who are exploring the full diversity of splat mechanics across a huge variety of splats, and also the richness of any given splat will lean players towards feeling satisfied with all playing a group of the same splat. In a simplified system then, your design incentives are going to be serving cross-splat play as a niche that's less easy to run in the main game, and where intra-splat play is a bit less rich niche to explore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T14:24:44-07:00","id":1382825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hurum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1382804#post1382804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would think their are other ways of &quot;evening up&quot; mixed groups than an all-round equaling of the power levels (what about bonus XP or increasing the cost of charms for the more potent Exalts when in a mixed group?)</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> A DB <i>player</i> need not be much weaker than a Solar one</div> </div> </div> </div>So I was thinking about the fact that DBs in 3rd ed start at E2, with the same number of charms and more merits than Solars. Now it's not like DBs actually start with E2 or that many charms, but that by default you play an experienced Dragonblood.<br /> <br /> And so, in terms of fluff and PCs/NPCs, I wonder if you can use that. Maybe DBs have charms that are just a bit weaker, and both DB and Solar PCs start with 10 charms, the same stats, and the DB gets more background-type stuff. Or maybe the DB even gets <i>more</i> stats and charms (but their charms are weaker). But a DB PC represents a Dragonblood who's exceptional or experienced (say, in their 50s), while the Solar represents a very new Solar.<br /> (And Lunar PCs, Sidereal PCs, Alchemical PCs, etc, represent something a bit more experienced than the Solar PC but not much more.)<br /> <br /> And so, in the setting, a Solar who's been exalted for 20 years is far more powerful than a Dragonblood who's been exalted for 20 years, but in terms of PCs there's only a bit of a difference.<br /> <br /> <br /> And you could also include rules for less experienced DBs that are not designed for mixed play.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So to expand on this a little, maybe your mixed game consists of:<br /> Solar Shonen Protagonist, 17 years old, exalted two months ago<br /> Lunar bro, 25 years old, exalted a few years ago, explains the Anathema stuff<br /> Dragonblood air-wizard, 100 years old, gives advice while stroking his beard<br /> Dragonblood kung-fu sifu, 60 years old, she teaches kung-fu to our shonen protagonist.<br /> Alchemical robo-nerd, she was made 20 years ago and met the group in their adventure<br /> <br /> Or some such.<br /> Most stories of bands of heroes, after all, don't actually have them all be the same level of experience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 04-20-2020, 05:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T14:59:03-07:00","id":1382829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1382815#post1382815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something worth noting too is that 3e and to some extent ExEss kind of go with PC-NPC asymmetry. This is kind of important too. A DB <i>player</i> need not be much weaker than a Solar one, while NPCs need only be as powerful or weak as needed for the kind of games being run. For a group of Celestials, the DBs need to be enough a challange to be mattering, but that depends on how many you want htere to be for that. For a Dragon-Blooded, the Anathema NPC should be a credible thret, but something in the boundaries of what you try to run. ANd since NPCs need not follow PC rules to the letter, this means that from game to game, what even the power leell of an Exalt might be is probably pretty different depending on how they're constructed. Especially if (like the game kind of is decding on now and with <b>Essence</b>) go all in on QC-style write-ups for NPCS.<br /> <br /> Like, power levels really in the end are meaningless in such an environment IMHO. And there's plenty of way sot show those levels sublty (dice caps, mote pools, access to universal stuff) than to just have a lot of effects of &quot;This, but sucks&quot; that often non-Solar Charms was written for a lot of th epast editions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you ! That's what I wanted to say when I said that, whatever the PC design, the NPC's design really need to follow up and let the ST (and the players) tell the story they want to tell about the setting (the powers of the protagonists, of the antagonists, of whatever you may encounter). There does not need to be one single &quot;PC and NPC power is like that&quot;, but rather tools for the ST to adjust the story to whatever the table wants to play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T15:13:17-07:00","id":1382832,"title":"","content":"That\u2019s true. I\u2019ve seen people complain that 3e finally makes Dragon-Blooded compellingly powerful and fun to play in mixed groups, but the canon on their numbers becomes insane with them at that power level. But it\u2019s easy enough to assume the rules for player characters and big name NPC badasses, don\u2019t reflect the average Dynast legionnaire. Just like how PCs (and major npcs they may be repeatedly tangling with) accumulate charms and essence through experience much faster than average Exalted, who could take over a century to hit Essence 3. Even within the Exalted, PCs are special.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T15:36:33-07:00","id":1382833,"title":"","content":"That certainly works for Solars.<br /> <br /> I have a 1600 year-old Lunar who is Essence 5. His new buddy is an 80 year old Solar, who is... Essence 5. And there's some 30-year old Solars who are Essence 5.<br /> <br /> But obviously that's not the same when you have DBs vs, say, Lunars...<br /> <br /> I did notice that Essence just says &quot;yeah, Solar PCs are better than Solar NPCs, they win ties.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T16:09:23-07:00","id":1382839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1382825#post1382825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So I was thinking about the fact that DBs in 3rd ed start at E2, with the same number of charms and more merits than Solars. Now it's not like DBs actually start with E2 or that many charms, but that by default you play an experienced Dragonblood.<br /> <br /> And so, in terms of fluff and PCs/NPCs, I wonder if you can use that. Maybe DBs have charms that are just a bit weaker, and both DB and Solar PCs start with 10 charms, the same stats, and the DB gets more background-type stuff. Or maybe the DB even gets <i>more</i> stats and charms (but their charms are weaker). But a DB PC represents a Dragonblood who's exceptional or experienced (say, in their 50s), while the Solar represents a very new Solar.<br /> (And Lunar PCs, Sidereal PCs, Alchemical PCs, etc, represent something a bit more experienced than the Solar PC but not much more.)<br /> <br /> And so, in the setting, a Solar who's been exalted for 20 years is far more powerful than a Dragonblood who's been exalted for 20 years, but in terms of PCs there's only a bit of a difference.<br /> <br /> <br /> And you could also include rules for less experienced DBs that are not designed for mixed play.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So to expand on this a little, maybe your mixed game consists of:<br /> Solar Shonen Protagonist, 17 years old, exalted two months ago<br /> Lunar bro, 25 years old, exalted a few years ago, explains the Anathema stuff<br /> Dragonblood air-wizard, 100 years old, gives advice while stroking his beard<br /> Dragonblood kung-fu sifu, 60 years old, she teaches kung-fu to our shonen protagonist.<br /> Alchemical robo-nerd, she was made 20 years ago and met the group in their adventure<br /> <br /> Or some such.<br /> Most stories of bands of heroes, after all, don't actually have them all be the same level of experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>Broad agreement with this.<br /> <br /> Two Things:<br /> 1. Ten Winds. (I can't read this without immediately thinking of Keychain of Creation.)<br /> 2. Dragon-Blooded. Like Spider-Man.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1382832#post1382832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That\u2019s true. I\u2019ve seen people complain that 3e finally makes Dragon-Blooded compellingly powerful and fun to play in mixed groups, but <b>the canon on their numbers becomes insane with them at that power level</b>. But it\u2019s easy enough to assume the rules for player characters and big name NPC badasses, don\u2019t reflect the average Dynast legionnaire. Just like how PCs (and major npcs they may be repeatedly tangling with) accumulate charms and essence through experience much faster than average Exalted, who could take over a century to hit Essence 3. Even within the Exalted, PCs are special.</div> </div> </div> </div>You've seen the Arena fights, right?<br /> <br /> Starting Solars can chunk entire Kinships at a time, five on one, in 3E.<br /> <br /> Yes, the PCs are special, and I broadly agree with your point that a random NPC Deeb of no narrative importance isn't going to be as powerful as a PC. But Dragon-Blooded power level is pretty much right where it should be.<br /> <br /> The Dragon-Blooded won the Usurpation and maintained the Wyld Hunt for two thousand years. That's credible under 3E. But Celestials are still WAY more powerful than DBs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 04-20-2020, 07:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T16:15:00-07:00","id":1382841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1382833#post1382833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That certainly works for Solars.<br /> <br /> I have a 1600 year-old Lunar who is Essence 5. His new buddy is an 80 year old Solar, who is... Essence 5. And there's some 30-year old Solars who are Essence 5.<br /> <br /> But obviously that's not the same when you have DBs vs, say, Lunars...<br /> <br /> I did notice that Essence just says &quot;yeah, Solar PCs are better than Solar NPCs, they win ties.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It can be the same as Lunars va DBs. You can have DB mooks who are Essence 1 as adults with just a few Charms as \u201cgeneric DBs\u201d unlike the exceptional epic hero DB player characters who can hold their own with Lunars by virtue of following PC rules.<br /> <br /> I know that\u2019s not the default assumption of the game, but it\u2019s easily doable, and some would argue fits the setting better with their numbers as described.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T16:33:31-07:00","id":1382845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1382841#post1382841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It can be the same as Lunars va DBs. You can have DB mooks who are Essence 1 as adults with just a few Charms as \u201cgeneric DBs\u201d unlike the exceptional epic hero DB player characters who can hold their own with Lunars by virtue of following PC rules.<br /> <br /> I know that\u2019s not the default assumption of the game, but it\u2019s easily doable, and some would argue fits the setting better with their numbers as described.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder how it would work in reverse. For example right now if your group of DBs is Wyld Hunting a Solar, and that Solar looks like the Wandering Deathknight, or Volfer, or Faka Kun then it's going to look like a total curbstomp. Unless Volfer has gotten himself some allies or something.<br /> <br /> Should NPC Solars/Lunars be buffed up from where they are with asymetric rules?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T17:23:34-07:00","id":1382852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1382845#post1382845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wonder how it would work in reverse. For example right now if your group of DBs is Wyld Hunting a Solar, and that Solar looks like the Wandering Deathknight, or Volfer, or Faka Kun then it's going to look like a total curbstomp. Unless Volfer has gotten himself some allies or something.<br /> <br /> Should NPC Solars/Lunars be buffed up from where they are with asymetric rules?</div> </div> </div> </div>if you\u2019re looking for an intense challenge for combat focused DB players, of course!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T17:54:59-07:00","id":1382860,"title":"","content":"I'm a little curious about the place of Alchemicals in Ex3 and what we might see of that in Exalted Essence.<br /> Since historically Autochthonia getting back in contact with Creation was kind of the original Reclamation level shake-up of the world and even with 2e downplaying the possibility of a Locust War the concensus in most of the game spaces I've been in towards their inclusion has been &quot;please, don't&quot; despite seeing how the Alchemicals themselves could be fun.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T19:09:28-07:00","id":1382873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1382860#post1382860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm a little curious about the place of Alchemicals in Ex3 and what we might see of that in Exalted Essence.<br /> Since historically Autochthonia getting back in contact with Creation was kind of the original Reclamation level shake-up of the world and even with 2e downplaying the possibility of a Locust War the concensus in most of the game spaces I've been in towards their inclusion has been &quot;please, don't&quot; despite seeing how the Alchemicals themselves could be fun.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>We address this explicitly in both Essence and Crucible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T19:47:54-07:00","id":1382882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1382860#post1382860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm a little curious about the place of Alchemicals in Ex3 and what we might see of that in Exalted Essence.<br /> Since historically Autochthonia getting back in contact with Creation was kind of the original Reclamation level shake-up of the world and even with 2e downplaying the possibility of a Locust War the concensus in most of the game spaces I've been in towards their inclusion has been &quot;please, don't&quot; despite seeing how the Alchemicals themselves could be fun.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The Galaxy Brain take that came up in a forum game I'm in is that the Autochthonians have arrived in Creation... And then they took over Gem, which is very much <i>not</i> blown up. The native Gemmites just kind of shrug and go with it, because a coup and change of command is kind of y'know same shit different day, and at least these shiny metal people give you rations at the end of the day without tying it to how much work you did, and if you get injured they pull you off the line and patch you up. Not GREAT but it's a step up.<br /> <br /> This is probably not the direction that Ex3 will take. :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-21T00:58:40-07:00","id":1382919,"title":"","content":"My ST did something similar. They conquered large parts of the South, then were pushed back and it settled down.<br /> <br /> In my game, they turned up with Autocthon to defeat the Second Balorian Crusade, then settled down with the 8 Nations in different parts of the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-21T08:55:11-07:00","id":1382978,"title":"","content":"<b>Neon Attack on Autochthonian Rim (campaign seed) [original thread <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1102697-neon-attack-on-autochthonian-rim-campaign-seed\">here</a>]</b><br /> <br /> The first Autochthonian nation to succeed at Project Razor suffers the misfortune to open a portal into the depths of one of Creation's oceans. The portal is closed as quickly as possible to prevent any more flooding and drowning.<br /> <br /> It's ultimately decided that adapting to this challenge would be more efficient than starting the project over from the beginning in the hopes of a different outcome. The portal-opening municipal Charm is moved and surrounded by an additional municipal Charm for containing the water, as well as channeling some of it into the Great Maker's systems.<br /> <br /> But the other side of the portal is discovered by a coven of warmongering Lunar Exalted, who have been using sorcery to create terrible amphibious behemoths for raiding and assaulting the Scarlet Dynasty's coastal assets. Using their sorcery and artifice, they seize control the portal and force it to remain open, and launch an attack.<br /> <br /> The hydraulic containment Charm and portal Charm are destroyed. The Metropolis is flooded, her citizens drowned to death, her Charms damaged, her infrastructure unmanned, and her very core captured and studied by horrible witches from another world. Unchecked, the behemoths and their Lunar masters emerge from the flooded chambers to attack the other cities of the Autochthonian nation.<br /> <br /> Every Champion and Colossus is refitted for war against this aquatic nightmare. The innards and fluids of the machine god quiver with the thunderous battle of metal giants against fleshy behemoths.<br /> <br /> One day, the Autochthonians succeed in killing one of the Lunar Exalted themselves, and Luna turns her eye upon them. She Chooses one of them to become her child's next incarnation. This new Lunar Exalt is so impacted by the image of the giant monsters attacking his home that his Spirit Shape is one of them. He transforms and single-handedly kills and devours one of the invading monsters in full view of his own people's warriors.<br /> <br /> Now his nation struggles to decide what to do him.<br /> <br /> <br /> The tone is primarily <i>Pacific Rim</i>. Each side is doing its earnest best to win.<br /> <br /> The &quot;designed to fail&quot; systems of <i>Attack On Titan</i> and <i>Neon Genesis Evangelion</i> have absolutely no place in Autochthonia; even the Sidereal Exalted back in Creation didn't design the Immaculate Order to fail. The powers that be in Autochthonia <i>really do</i> want the invaders repelled and defeated, and the powers attacking them <i>really do</i> want to conquer them. Different factions have different ideas about the best ways to do that, or about how important it is or how much it will cost, but there's no conspiracy on either side tricking their nominal allies into self-defeating patterns to create an ever-lasting war.<br /> <br /> That trope seems to come up a lot in Japanese stories. A reaction against their government?<br /> <br /> <br /> Still, while the primary inspiration is <i>Pacific Rim</i>, I wanted to cast a wide net for superficially similar franchises, to give storytellers and players a buffet of choices.<br /> <br /> Warstriders are probably in short supply in Autochthonia, where Colossi serve the role much better and with a lot more flexibility in function. Some storytellers might be willing to let their players be elder-level Alchemical Exalted with the bodies of giants.<br /> <br /> Other storytellers might be more comfortable having Colossi function as particularly willful warstriders for players with Champion-level Exalted, like BT from <i>Titanfall 2</i>. These Colossi wanted more power in battle, and so chose members of their younger brethren to serve as their <a href=\"http://tfwiki.net/wiki/Headmaster_(technology)\" target=\"_blank\">headmasters </a>or <a href=\"http://tfwiki.net/wiki/Powermaster\" target=\"_blank\">powermasters</a>.<br /> <br /> Some players might want to fight the Titans/Kaiju as man-sized Champions equipped with high-mobility Charms and/or artifacts.<br /> <br /> The possibility of an Autochthonian Lunar lets a player get to be Godzilla (though Gamera might be more apt), or Eren Jaeger and his titan form, or <a href=\"http://heroicage.wikia.com/wiki/Bellcross\" target=\"_blank\">Age and Bellcross</a>, or a particularly different variation on Shinji Ikari and Eva-01.<br /> <br /> Someone who wants to play an Adamant Caste or other Alchemical spy could have a story about thwarting the subtler invasion attempts of a face-stealing skinwalker who infiltrates the Autochthonian nation to steal its secrets and wound it from within.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 04-21-2020, 11:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-21T11:03:28-07:00","id":1383004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1382839#post1382839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two Things:<br /> 1. Ten Winds. (I can't read this without immediately thinking of Keychain of Creation.)<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I thought of Keychain as I was writing it. Keychain is basically pretty perfect for a mixed-circle. The Solar and Abyssal are pretty young. The Lunar is slightly older. And then the wise Immaculate Master is much more experienced.<br /> <br /> And I guess, tbh, in the very mixed game I play, the Solars and Lunar have been exalted for 2 or 3 years, my Dragonblood's been exalted for like 20 years, and the other Dragonblood I think is much older.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. Dragon-Blooded. Like Spider-Man. </div> </div> </div>As in, their power is much less than Captain America/Dr Strange/the Hulk/etc but they're still useful?<br /> <br /> (One key thing I think with Spider-Man is that he's specialised in speed and agility, and the others in the Avengers who specialise in speed and agility are all low-power.<br /> Whereas the more powerful Avengers are specialised in intelligence/science or power/toughness or magic.<br /> Except when Quicksilver was an Avenger I guess. )","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-21T11:08:39-07:00","id":1383005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1383004#post1383004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As in, their power is much less than Captain America/Dr Strange/the Hulk/etc but they're still useful?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://i.pinimg.com/originals/b2/0f/05/b20f05be115bdf760e50ec4ab1724afd.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Not quite that.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T19:35:28-07:00","id":1383274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElfSpeaker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1381042#post1381042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Quick correction, Monica has played a ton of Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>For perspective, I have Exalted homebrew documents from her in my googled drive dated January 1st 1970 not only does this predate the release of 1st edition but also well before either of us were born. <b>That</b> is how much Exalted Monica has played.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T23:09:28-07:00","id":1383298,"title":"","content":"That is a lot, not going to lie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-02T11:35:45-07:00","id":1385279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1383274#post1383274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For perspective, I have Exalted homebrew documents from her in my googled drive dated January 1st 1970 not only does this predate the release of 1st edition but also well before either of us were born. <b>That</b> is how much Exalted Monica has played.<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>No! <i><b>NO!!</b></i> You weren't supposed to reveal that! You've doomed us all!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26122-seraswinterblood","name":"seraswinterblood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26122_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-02T19:17:24-07:00","id":1385340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>seraswinterblood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1385279#post1385279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No! <i><b>NO!!</b></i> You weren't supposed to reveal that! You've doomed us all!</div> </div> </div> </div>Seras! Fancy seeing you outside of The Freedomstone. Haven't been there since Keychain of Creation stopped updating.<br /> <br /> You probably won't remember me; I don't think we talked all that much, and I can't remember if I called myself Inugami or Tornado Wolf at the time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T12:46:48-07:00","id":1385902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>seraswinterblood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1385279#post1385279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No! <i><b>NO!!</b></i> You weren't supposed to reveal that! You've doomed us all!</div> </div> </div> </div>Upside is that we might get a do-over on 2020 when time unravels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T13:28:17-07:00","id":1385915,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I am pretty sick of living in the Mirror Universe. I want to move to the normal timeline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T14:33:00-07:00","id":1385940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1385915#post1385915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I am pretty sick of living in the Mirror Universe. I want to move to the normal timeline.</div> </div> </div> </div>You haven't seen anything yet.<br /> <br /> This will not stop. This will not slow down. Things will improve, but change itself will only accelerate.<br /> <br /> The old normal is dead, and that's good. The old normal wasn't working.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T14:48:42-07:00","id":1385945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview?p=1385940#post1385940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You haven't seen anything yet.<br /> <br /> This will not stop. This will not slow down. Things will improve, but change itself will only accelerate.<br /> <br /> The old normal is dead, and that's good. The old normal wasn't working.</div> </div> </div> </div>Certainly technological and economic changes aren't going to slow down - but the normalcy of &quot;the President of the US is smart enough not to bring up injecting people with household cleaners to fight a virus on live television&quot; I don't think is too much for anyone to ask for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T15:04:34-07:00","id":13859